-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Adam.Opt.Loops.adam - the loop passes (M6 O11 on): loop form, licm,
  indvars and loopshape

  FormLoops puts every loop it can shape in the form each loop pass starts
  from (every loop pass calls it first):
    preheader  the header's one entry from outside the loop: a block that
               only jumps to it, in the header's scopes (a new block takes
               every outside edge otherwise; the header's phis then get one
               value from it, a phi of the new block when the edges brought
               more than one)
    latch      one back edge: a new block takes every back edge when there
               are more (the header's phis get one value from it the same
               way)
    exits      dedicated: every block a loop edge leaves to has only loop
               blocks before it (a new block takes the loop's edges to it
               otherwise)
    lcssa      a value the loop makes that a block outside it uses reaches
               that use through a phi in an exit block, and through the
               phis an SSA update places where the exits' values meet;
               innermost loops first, so an outer loop closes the phis an
               inner one made
  A loop is shaped only when its header is not the entry and no scope
  resumes at it (an unwind edge cannot be moved); its exits and lcssa only
  when no unwind edge leaves it. A value is closed only when every block
  from its uses back to the exits is reached and no resume block (a phi
  can go there); else it keeps its uses (a use in a block the entry does
  not reach is left alone). A new block goes beside a block whose scopes it
  takes (the header, the exit it leads to): it joins every scope that block
  is in and no other, every position after it moves on by one, so each
  scope's run stays a run and its resume block its own.

  HoistInvariants is licm, innermost loops first: an instruction of the
  loop whose operands are all made outside it (or moved out already) goes
  to the end of the preheader, before its jump, when it is
    pure     an integer / float / compare / convert / offset op, a
             constant or an address, or a call of a routine that is pure
             and nothrow (Adam.Opt.Facts); a threadaddr only from a loop
             with no call (G1d0: the running thread's copy holds only up to
             the next call, one may switch the fiber to another thread)
    a load   whose address is invariant, in a loop no scope resumes in, not
             of a slot a funclet reaches, and that no store, copy, fill,
             atomic or call of the loop may write: two accesses are apart
             when their bases are distinct slots, distinct data or
             threadstatics, or one base with constant ranges apart; a call
             or an unknown pointer reaches anything but a slot whose
             address never leaves its loads, stores, copies and fills
  and, when it may fault (a load not known valid, a division by a value
  that may fault: Adam.Opt.DCE's rule), only from the header, ahead of any
  instruction there that has a side effect or may fault and stays: the
  preheader runs exactly when the header first does, in the same scopes,
  so the fault comes at the same moment. A check (its compare, branch and
  raise) never moves ahead of a side effect: branches and calls never
  move. A moved value still dominates its uses (the preheader dominates
  the loop); nothing moves out of a loop with no preheader.

  SimplifyInductions is indvars, innermost loops first, over each loop
  with a preheader and one latch. A basic induction variable is a header
  phi that starts at a value from the preheader and steps by a constant
  (an add or a sub of the phi) on the latch's edge. Its exit test is a
  loop block's branch on a compare of the phi with an invariant limit, one
  edge staying in the loop, the other leaving it, the block it stays to
  entered from the test alone and dominating the latch: every next turn
  passes the test. From a constant start and limit it knows the
  variable's range, in the blocks the stay block dominates (the test held)
  and in the whole loop (it never steps past its last value, so it never
  wraps), and from them:
    checks     a loop block's branch on a compare of values whose ranges
               decide it (constants, the variables, converts, adds, subs,
               multiplies and shifts by constants, ands with a constant,
               none wrapping) gets that constant: an index check the range
               proves can never fail goes once simplifycfg folds it (the
               same behaviour at every level)
    exits      on the test's exit edge a not-equal test's variable equals
               its limit (a less / greater test's its last value, from
               constants): the exit phis take that value for it
    reduction  an address an invariant base moves by an affine count of a
               variable (a multiple of it plus a constant, at 64 bits; a
               narrower variable only widened within its range) with a
               multiply or shift in it becomes a pointer phi of the
               header: the first turn's address made in the preheader, a
               step by the count's stride made in the latch
    merging    a variable that steps by the same constant as another of
               its type (the one the exit test reads is kept) is that one
               plus the difference of their starts, exact as both wrap
               alike
  No block and no edge is added or removed: the loops keep their form.

  ShapeLoops is loopshape (fast only: it trades size for speed), one shape
  at a time, the facts and the loop form made again after each, at most
  ADAM_LOOPS_MAX_SHAPES a function. It takes an innermost loop with a
  preheader and one latch, every block reached, none a resume block, no
  unwind edge out, no slot, parameter or varargs start in it, every block
  ending in a jump or a branch, and every value it makes closed (a use
  outside it is an exit phi's operand from a loop block): such a loop can
  be copied, a copy's block beside its original in that block's scopes, its
  values and blocks the copy's, the exits' phis given the copy's entries.
  Each loop header tries each shape once, in this order:
    unswitch   a branch of the loop on a condition made outside it: the
               loop copied, the copy reading it false and the loop true,
               the preheader's jump a branch on it between the two
    full       the loop's one exiting block, passed every turn, ends in a
               branch its turns decide: a constant, a header phi (its
               preheader value, then its back edge value of the turn
               before), adds and subs, wrapped as the machine does, and
               their compares; the turns up to the one it leaves in laid
               out in a row, each copy's branch a known bool (simplifycfg
               folds them: the back edge goes, the loop is straight code)
    rotate     a header that tests (a branch to a stay block entered from
               it alone and out of the loop) copied before it: the copy is
               the first test, the header the test at the end of each turn,
               a header value used past it merged with its copy's by a phi
               of the stay block (the new header)
    partial    the body laid out up to ADAM_LOOPS_PARTIAL_COPIES times in a
               row, each copy keeping its own exit tests: exact for any trip
               count, with no remainder loop
  A copy's header has the copy before it as its one predecessor: its phis
  take one value, the back edge value of that copy; the loop's header takes
  the last copy's. Every shape keeps what the program does at every turn.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit Adam.Opt.Loops;

import System.SysUtils, Adam.Core.Containers, Adam.Backend.SSA, Adam.Opt.Analysis,
  Adam.Opt.Facts;

const
  // No block / no instruction / no value (a map's missing value)
  ADAM_LOOPS_NONE: int64 = -1;
  // A slot's escape mark (InvariantHoister.DoSlotFact): its address stays in its loads,
  // stores, copies and fills; it leaves them; a funclet reaches it
  ADAM_LOOPS_KEPT: int64 = 0;
  ADAM_LOOPS_ESCAPED: int64 = 1;
  ADAM_LOOPS_FUNCLET: int64 = 2;
  // What an address's base is: a slot, a data blob, a threadstatic, any other pointer
  ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_SLOT: int64 = 0;
  ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_DATA: int64 = 1;
  ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_THREAD: int64 = 2;
  ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_OTHER: int64 = 3;
  // An access whose byte count is not known (an atomic's place)
  ADAM_LOOPS_ANY_SIZE: int64 = -1;
  // indvars' bounds (InductionSimplifier): every range end it keeps (2^62), a factor or a
  // range end a product may take (2^31), an affine count's scale or constant (2^30), the
  // largest constant shift it reads as a multiply, how deep a range or affine walk goes,
  // and how many addresses one loop has reduced
  ADAM_LOOPS_RANGE_CAP: int64 = 4611686018427387904;
  ADAM_LOOPS_PRODUCT_CAP: int64 = 2147483648;
  ADAM_LOOPS_AFFINE_CAP: int64 = 1073741824;
  ADAM_LOOPS_MAX_SHIFT: int64 = 30;
  ADAM_LOOPS_WALK_DEPTH: int64 = 16;
  ADAM_LOOPS_MAX_REDUCED: int64 = 8;
  // What an induction variable is on its exit test's exit edge (InductionFact.ExitKind):
  // not known, a value of the function, a constant
  ADAM_LOOPS_EXIT_NONE: int64 = 0;
  ADAM_LOOPS_EXIT_VALUE: int64 = 1;
  ADAM_LOOPS_EXIT_CONSTANT: int64 = 2;
  // loopshape's bounds (LoopShaper): the most turns a full unroll lays out and the
  // instructions it may make (turns times the loop's size), a partial unroll's most copies
  // and the instructions they may make, the largest header a rotation copies, the largest
  // loop unswitching copies, and the most shapes one function takes
  ADAM_LOOPS_FULL_TURNS: int64 = 16;
  ADAM_LOOPS_FULL_BUDGET: int64 = 256;
  ADAM_LOOPS_PARTIAL_COPIES: int64 = 4;
  ADAM_LOOPS_PARTIAL_BUDGET: int64 = 64;
  ADAM_LOOPS_ROTATE_SIZE: int64 = 16;
  ADAM_LOOPS_UNSWITCH_SIZE: int64 = 64;
  ADAM_LOOPS_MAX_SHAPES: int64 = 16;
  // Raised (an invariant broken): a block that ends in no terminator; a loop form that does
  // not settle
  ADAM_LOOPS_FAULT_NO_TERMINATOR: string = "Opt: loops found a block with no terminator: b";
  ADAM_LOOPS_FAULT_UNSETTLED: string = "Opt: loops did not settle the loop form of f";

// The terminator of the block ABlock (an id); raised when it ends in none
func DoTerminatorOf(const AModule: ref IRModule; const ABlock: int64): ref IRInstr;
var
  LInstrs: ref Int64List;
  LLast: ref IRInstr;
begin
  LInstrs := AModule.BlockAt(ABlock).Instrs;
  if LInstrs.Count = 0 then
    raise(ADAM_LOOPS_FAULT_NO_TERMINATOR + IntToStr(ABlock));
  end;
  LLast := AModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LInstrs.Count - 1]);
  if not IsTerminator(LLast.Kind) then
    raise(ADAM_LOOPS_FAULT_NO_TERMINATOR + IntToStr(ABlock));
  end;
  return LLast;
end;

// True when the block at APosition is in the run of AFunction's scope AIndex
func DoInScope(const AFunction: ref IRFunction; const AIndex: int64;
  const APosition: int64): bool;
begin
  return (AFunction.ScopeFirst(AIndex) <= APosition) and
    (APosition <= AFunction.ScopeLast(AIndex));
end;

// True when the blocks at APosition and AOther are in the same scopes
func DoSameScopes(const AFunction: ref IRFunction; const APosition: int64;
  const AOther: int64): bool;
var
  LK: int64;
begin
  for LK := 0 to AFunction.ScopeCount() - 1 do
    if DoInScope(AFunction, LK, APosition) then
      if not DoInScope(AFunction, LK, AOther) then
        return false;
      end;
    else
      if DoInScope(AFunction, LK, AOther) then
        return false;
      end;
    end;
  end;
  return true;
end;

// True when a scope of AFunction resumes at the block at APosition (an unwind edge runs
// into it)
func DoIsResume(const AFunction: ref IRFunction; const APosition: int64): bool;
var
  LK: int64;
begin
  for LK := 0 to AFunction.ScopeCount() - 1 do
    if AFunction.ScopeTarget(LK) = APosition then
      return true;
    end;
  end;
  return false;
end;

// A new phi of AType (its node ANode, no entries yet) at the front of the block ABlock (an
// id); returns its id
func DoNewPhi(const AModule: ref IRModule; const ABlock: int64; const AType: IRType;
  const ANode: int64): int64;
var
  LBlock: ref IRBlock;
  LKept: ref Int64List;
  LPhi: int64;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LPhi := AModule.Emit(ABlock, IROp.Phi, AType, ANode);
  // Emit put it last: the block's list made again with it first
  LBlock := AModule.BlockAt(ABlock);
  LKept := ref Int64List();
  LKept.Add(LPhi);
  for LI := 0 to LBlock.Instrs.Count - 2 do
    LKept.Add(LBlock.Instrs[LI]);
  end;
  LBlock.Instrs := LKept;
  return LPhi;
end;

// The node a new block's jump to ATarget (a block id) takes: ATarget's first instruction's
func DoNodeOf(const AModule: ref IRModule; const ATarget: int64): int64;
var
  LInstrs: ref Int64List;
begin
  LInstrs := AModule.BlockAt(ATarget).Instrs;
  if LInstrs.Count = 0 then
    return 0;
  end;
  return AModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[0]).Node;
end;

// A new instruction (AKind, AType, ANode) in the block ABlock (an id), just before its
// terminator; returns its id
func DoEmitAtEnd(const AModule: ref IRModule; const ABlock: int64; const AKind: IROp;
  const AType: IRType; const ANode: int64): int64;
var
  LBlock: ref IRBlock;
  LPlaced: ref Int64List;
  LId: int64;
  LCount: int64;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LId := AModule.Emit(ABlock, AKind, AType, ANode);
  // Emit put it last, after the terminator: the list made again with it before that
  LBlock := AModule.BlockAt(ABlock);
  LCount := LBlock.Instrs.Count;
  LPlaced := ref Int64List();
  for LI := 0 to LCount - 3 do
    LPlaced.Add(LBlock.Instrs[LI]);
  end;
  LPlaced.Add(LId);
  LPlaced.Add(LBlock.Instrs[LCount - 2]);
  LBlock.Instrs := LPlaced;
  return LId;
end;

// The edges from the blocks APreds (ids) to ATarget (a block id) moved to a new block that
// only jumps to ATarget, put beside the block at AAnchor (ABefore as IRModule.InsertBlock):
// each phi of ATarget takes one value from the new block (the one the moved edges brought
// when they all brought one, else a new phi of the new block over them); returns its id
func DoSplitEdges(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
  const ATarget: int64; const APreds: ref Int64List; const AAnchor: int64;
  const ABefore: bool): int64;
var
  LTargetInstrs: ref Int64List;
  LOperands: ref Int64List;
  LTargets: ref Int64List;
  LMoved: ref Int64List;
  LFrom: ref Int64List;
  LPhi: ref IRInstr;
  LMerge: ref IRInstr;
  LTerm: ref IRInstr;
  LSame: bool;
  LNew: int64;
  LJump: int64;
  LMergeId: int64;
  LValue: int64;
  LI: int64;
  LK: int64;
  LE: int64;
begin
  LNew := AModule.InsertBlock(AFunction, AAnchor, ABefore);
  LTargetInstrs := AModule.BlockAt(ATarget).Instrs;
  for LK := 0 to LTargetInstrs.Count - 1 do
    LPhi := AModule.InstrAt(LTargetInstrs[LK]);
    if LPhi.Kind <> IROp.Phi then
      skip;
    end;
    LOperands := ref Int64List();
    LTargets := ref Int64List();
    LMoved := ref Int64List();
    LFrom := ref Int64List();
    for LE := 0 to LPhi.Targets.Count - 1 do
      if APreds.IndexOf(LPhi.Targets[LE]) >= 0 then
        LMoved.Add(LPhi.Operands[LE]);
        LFrom.Add(LPhi.Targets[LE]);
      else
        LOperands.Add(LPhi.Operands[LE]);
        LTargets.Add(LPhi.Targets[LE]);
      end;
    end;
    if LMoved.Count = 0 then
      skip;
    end;
    LSame := true;
    for LE := 1 to LMoved.Count - 1 do
      if LMoved[LE] <> LMoved[0] then
        LSame := false;
      end;
    end;
    if LSame then
      LValue := LMoved[0];
    else
      // The new block's phis come before its jump (emitted below)
      LMergeId := AModule.Emit(LNew, IROp.Phi, LPhi.ValueType, LPhi.Node);
      LMerge := AModule.InstrAt(LMergeId);
      for LE := 0 to LMoved.Count - 1 do
        LMerge.Operands.Add(LMoved[LE]);
        LMerge.Targets.Add(LFrom[LE]);
      end;
      LValue := LMergeId;
    end;
    LOperands.Add(LValue);
    LTargets.Add(LNew);
    LPhi.Operands := LOperands;
    LPhi.Targets := LTargets;
  end;
  LJump := AModule.Emit(LNew, IROp.Jump, IRType.Void, DoNodeOf(AModule, ATarget));
  AModule.InstrAt(LJump).Targets.Add(ATarget);
  for LI := 0 to APreds.Count - 1 do
    LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(AModule, APreds[LI]);
    for LE := 0 to LTerm.Targets.Count - 1 do
      if LTerm.Targets[LE] = ATarget then
        LTerm.Targets[LE] := LNew;
      end;
    end;
  end;
  return LNew;
end;

// True when the loop AIndex can be shaped (see the header): its header is not the entry
// and no scope resumes at it
func DoShapeable(const AFunction: ref IRFunction; const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis;
  const AIndex: int64): bool;
var
  LHeader: int64;
begin
  LHeader := AAnalysis.LoopHeader(AIndex);
  return (LHeader <> 0) and (not DoIsResume(AFunction, LHeader));
end;

// One mark per block position of a function of ACount blocks: true for the loop AIndex's
func DoLoopSet(const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis; const ACount: int64;
  const AIndex: int64): BoolArray;
var
  LIn: BoolArray;
  LBlocks: ref Int64List;
  LI: int64;
begin
  setlength(LIn, ACount);
  for LI := 0 to ACount - 1 do
    LIn[LI] := false;
  end;
  LBlocks := AAnalysis.LoopBlocks(AIndex);
  for LI := 0 to LBlocks.Count - 1 do
    LIn[LBlocks[LI]] := true;
  end;
  return LIn;
end;

// The deepest loop depth of AAnalysis's function (0: no loop)
func DoMaxDepth(const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis): int64;
var
  LMax: int64;
  LL: int64;
begin
  LMax := 0;
  for LL := 0 to AAnalysis.LoopCount() - 1 do
    if AAnalysis.LoopDepth(LL) > LMax then
      LMax := AAnalysis.LoopDepth(LL);
    end;
  end;
  return LMax;
end;

// The preheader of the loop AIndex (its blocks AIn) as a position (ADAM_LOOPS_NONE: it has
// none): the header's one predecessor from outside the loop, reached, a block that only
// jumps to the header, in the header's scopes. Inside a protected scope every block has
// that scope's unwind edge (Adam.Opt.Analysis): a preheader in the header's scopes has
// the header's own, so only its other successors count (counting them all kept a loop in
// a guard from ever settling: a new preheader was split off at every step)
func DoPreheaderOf(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: ref IRFunction;
  const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis; const AIndex: int64; const AIn: BoolArray): int64;
var
  LPreds: ref Int64List;
  LHeader: int64;
  LOutside: int64;
  LCount: int64;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LHeader := AAnalysis.LoopHeader(AIndex);
  LPreds := AAnalysis.PredsOf(LHeader);
  LCount := 0;
  LOutside := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
  for LI := 0 to LPreds.Count - 1 do
    if not AIn[LPreds[LI]] then
      LCount := LCount + 1;
      LOutside := LPreds[LI];
    end;
  end;
  if LCount <> 1 then
    return ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
  end;
  if not AAnalysis.Reachable(LOutside) then
    return ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
  end;
  if AAnalysis.SuccsOf(LOutside).Count - AAnalysis.UnwindSuccsOf(LOutside).Count <> 1 then
    return ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
  end;
  if DoTerminatorOf(AModule, AAnalysis.BlockAt(LOutside)).Kind <> IROp.Jump then
    return ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
  end;
  if not DoSameScopes(AFunction, LOutside, LHeader) then
    return ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
  end;
  return LOutside;
end;

// True when an unwind edge leaves the loop AIndex (its blocks AIn): its exits cannot move
func DoUnwindExit(const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis; const AIndex: int64;
  const AIn: BoolArray): bool;
var
  LBlocks: ref Int64List;
  LUnwind: ref Int64List;
  LI: int64;
  LK: int64;
begin
  LBlocks := AAnalysis.LoopBlocks(AIndex);
  for LI := 0 to LBlocks.Count - 1 do
    LUnwind := AAnalysis.UnwindSuccsOf(LBlocks[LI]);
    for LK := 0 to LUnwind.Count - 1 do
      if not AIn[LUnwind[LK]] then
        return true;
      end;
    end;
  end;
  return false;
end;

// One step of the loop form (see the header): the first loop that lacks a preheader, one
// latch or a dedicated exit gets it (one new block); false when every loop has its form
func DoShapeStep(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
  const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis): bool;
var
  LFunction: ref IRFunction;
  LIn: BoolArray;
  LBlocks: ref Int64List;
  LPreds: ref Int64List;
  LSuccs: ref Int64List;
  LMoved: ref Int64List;
  LOutside: bool;
  LCount: int64;
  LHeader: int64;
  LExit: int64;
  LL: int64;
  LI: int64;
  LK: int64;
  LE: int64;
begin
  LFunction := AModule.FunctionAt(AFunction);
  LCount := LFunction.Blocks.Count;
  for LL := 0 to AAnalysis.LoopCount() - 1 do
    if not DoShapeable(LFunction, AAnalysis, LL) then
      skip;
    end;
    LIn := DoLoopSet(AAnalysis, LCount, LL);
    LHeader := AAnalysis.LoopHeader(LL);
    LPreds := AAnalysis.PredsOf(LHeader);
    // The preheader: every edge from outside moved to a new block before the header
    if DoPreheaderOf(AModule, LFunction, AAnalysis, LL, LIn) = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
      LMoved := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to LPreds.Count - 1 do
        if not LIn[LPreds[LI]] then
          LMoved.Add(AAnalysis.BlockAt(LPreds[LI]));
        end;
      end;
      DoSplitEdges(AModule, AFunction, AAnalysis.BlockAt(LHeader), LMoved, LHeader, true);
      return true;
    end;
    // One latch: every back edge moved to a new block after the header
    LMoved := ref Int64List();
    for LI := 0 to LPreds.Count - 1 do
      if LIn[LPreds[LI]] then
        LMoved.Add(AAnalysis.BlockAt(LPreds[LI]));
      end;
    end;
    if LMoved.Count > 1 then
      DoSplitEdges(AModule, AFunction, AAnalysis.BlockAt(LHeader), LMoved, LHeader, false);
      return true;
    end;
    // Dedicated exits: an exit with a block outside the loop before it gets a new block
    // that takes the loop's edges to it
    if DoUnwindExit(AAnalysis, LL, LIn) then
      skip;
    end;
    LBlocks := AAnalysis.LoopBlocks(LL);
    for LI := 0 to LBlocks.Count - 1 do
      LSuccs := AAnalysis.SuccsOf(LBlocks[LI]);
      for LK := 0 to LSuccs.Count - 1 do
        LExit := LSuccs[LK];
        if LIn[LExit] then
          skip;
        end;
        LPreds := AAnalysis.PredsOf(LExit);
        LOutside := false;
        LMoved := ref Int64List();
        for LE := 0 to LPreds.Count - 1 do
          if LIn[LPreds[LE]] then
            LMoved.Add(AAnalysis.BlockAt(LPreds[LE]));
          else
            LOutside := true;
          end;
        end;
        if LOutside then
          // The entry cannot have a block put before it (it stays first)
          DoSplitEdges(AModule, AFunction, AAnalysis.BlockAt(LExit), LMoved, LExit,
            LExit <> 0);
          return true;
        end;
      end;
    end;
  end;
  return false;
end;

type
  // The lcssa of one loop of a function (see the header): each value the loop makes and
  // a block outside it uses, closed through its exits' phis
  LoopCloser = object
    hidden FModule: ref IRModule;
    hidden FFunction: ref IRFunction;
    hidden FFunctionId: int64;
    hidden FAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis;
    // The loop's blocks, its exits (positions) and whether a position is one
    hidden FIn: BoolArray;
    hidden FExits: ref Int64List;
    hidden FIsExit: BoolArray;
    // The value being closed, its type and node, and the value each block (by position)
    // starts with in its closed form (ADAM_LOOPS_NONE: not made yet)
    hidden FValue: int64;
    hidden FType: IRType;
    hidden FNode: int64;
    hidden FValueAt: Int64Array;

    // The closing of AModule's function AFunction's loops, its facts AAnalysis
    init(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
      const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis);
    begin
      self.FModule := AModule;
      self.FFunction := AModule.FunctionAt(AFunction);
      self.FFunctionId := AFunction;
      self.FAnalysis := AAnalysis;
      self.FExits := ref Int64List();
      self.FValue := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FType := IRType.Void;
      self.FNode := 0;
    end;

    // The exits of the loop AIndex into FExits / FIsExit; false when one has a block
    // outside the loop before it, is a resume block or is not reached
    hidden method DoExits(const AIndex: int64): bool;
    var
      LBlocks: ref Int64List;
      LSuccs: ref Int64List;
      LPreds: ref Int64List;
      LExit: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      setlength(self.FIsExit, len(self.FIn));
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FIn) - 1 do
        self.FIsExit[LI] := false;
      end;
      self.FExits := ref Int64List();
      LBlocks := self.FAnalysis.LoopBlocks(AIndex);
      for LI := 0 to LBlocks.Count - 1 do
        LSuccs := self.FAnalysis.SuccsOf(LBlocks[LI]);
        for LK := 0 to LSuccs.Count - 1 do
          LExit := LSuccs[LK];
          if (not self.FIn[LExit]) and (not self.FIsExit[LExit]) then
            self.FIsExit[LExit] := true;
            self.FExits.Add(LExit);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FExits.Count - 1 do
        LExit := self.FExits[LI];
        if DoIsResume(self.FFunction, LExit) or (not self.FAnalysis.Reachable(LExit)) then
          return false;
        end;
        LPreds := self.FAnalysis.PredsOf(LExit);
        for LK := 0 to LPreds.Count - 1 do
          if not self.FIn[LPreds[LK]] then
            return false;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // True when a phi can go at every block from the places APlaces (positions outside
    // the loop) back to the exits: each reached, no resume block, not the entry, every
    // predecessor reached
    hidden const method DoClosable(const APlaces: ref Int64List): bool;
    var
      LSeen: BoolArray;
      LWork: ref Int64List;
      LPreds: ref Int64List;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      setlength(LSeen, len(self.FIn));
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FIn) - 1 do
        LSeen[LI] := false;
      end;
      LWork := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to APlaces.Count - 1 do
        LWork.Add(APlaces[LI]);
      end;
      while LWork.Count > 0 do
        LAt := LWork.RemoveLast();
        if LSeen[LAt] then
          skip;
        end;
        LSeen[LAt] := true;
        if self.FIsExit[LAt] then
          skip;
        end;
        // A block outside the loop with a loop block before it is an exit: never here
        if self.FIn[LAt] or (LAt = 0) or (not self.FAnalysis.Reachable(LAt)) or
          DoIsResume(self.FFunction, LAt) then
          return false;
        end;
        LPreds := self.FAnalysis.PredsOf(LAt);
        for LI := 0 to LPreds.Count - 1 do
          if not self.FAnalysis.Reachable(LPreds[LI]) then
            return false;
          end;
          LWork.Add(LPreds[LI]);
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The value FValue's closed form has at the start of the block APosition (its end as
    // well: nothing outside the loop makes it again): an exit's phi of FValue, a lone
    // predecessor's value, or a phi over the predecessors' values (made before them, so a
    // cycle meets it)
    hidden method DoValueAt(const APosition: int64): int64;
    var
      LPreds: ref Int64List;
      LPhi: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.FValueAt[APosition] <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
        return self.FValueAt[APosition];
      end;
      LPreds := self.FAnalysis.PredsOf(APosition);
      if self.FIsExit[APosition] then
        LPhi := DoNewPhi(self.FModule, self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(APosition), self.FType,
          self.FNode);
        for LI := 0 to LPreds.Count - 1 do
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Operands.Add(self.FValue);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Targets.Add(self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LPreds[LI]));
        end;
        self.FValueAt[APosition] := LPhi;
        return LPhi;
      end;
      if LPreds.Count = 1 then
        LValue := self.DoValueAt(LPreds[0]);
        self.FValueAt[APosition] := LValue;
        return LValue;
      end;
      LPhi := DoNewPhi(self.FModule, self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(APosition), self.FType,
        self.FNode);
      self.FValueAt[APosition] := LPhi;
      for LI := 0 to LPreds.Count - 1 do
        LValue := self.DoValueAt(LPreds[LI]);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Operands.Add(LValue);
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Targets.Add(self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LPreds[LI]));
      end;
      return LPhi;
    end;

    // The position a use of AId by AUser at operand AEntry is made at (a phi's: the block
    // the value arrives from); ADAM_LOOPS_NONE when it is not to be closed (in the loop,
    // not reached, another function's)
    hidden const method DoOutsidePlace(const AUser: ref IRInstr; const AEntry: int64): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      if self.FModule.BlockAt(AUser.Block).Owner <> self.FFunctionId then
        return ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      end;
      if AUser.Kind = IROp.Phi then
        LAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(AUser.Targets[AEntry]);
      else
        LAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(AUser.Block);
      end;
      if (LAt < 0) or self.FIn[LAt] or (not self.FAnalysis.Reachable(LAt)) then
        return ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      end;
      return LAt;
    end;

    // The value AId (of the loop) closed: every use outside the loop takes its closed form;
    // false when none is outside or it cannot be closed (DoClosable)
    hidden method DoCloseValue(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LUses: ref Int64List;
      LPlaces: ref Int64List;
      LDone: ref Int64Map;
      LUser: ref IRInstr;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      LUses := self.FAnalysis.UsesOf(AId);
      LPlaces := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to LUses.Count - 1 do
        LUser := self.FModule.InstrAt(LUses[LI]);
        for LE := 0 to LUser.Operands.Count - 1 do
          if LUser.Operands[LE] = AId then
            LAt := self.DoOutsidePlace(LUser, LE);
            if LAt <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
              LPlaces.Add(LAt);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if LPlaces.Count = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      if not self.DoClosable(LPlaces) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FValue := AId;
      self.FType := self.FModule.InstrAt(AId).ValueType;
      self.FNode := self.FModule.InstrAt(AId).Node;
      setlength(self.FValueAt, len(self.FIn));
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FIn) - 1 do
        self.FValueAt[LI] := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      end;
      // Each user once (the list has it once per operand it fills)
      LDone := ref Int64Map(ADAM_LOOPS_NONE);
      for LI := 0 to LUses.Count - 1 do
        if LDone.Find(LUses[LI]) <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
          skip;
        end;
        LDone.Put(LUses[LI], 1);
        LUser := self.FModule.InstrAt(LUses[LI]);
        for LE := 0 to LUser.Operands.Count - 1 do
          if LUser.Operands[LE] = AId then
            LAt := self.DoOutsidePlace(LUser, LE);
            if LAt <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
              LUser.Operands[LE] := self.DoValueAt(LAt);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The loop AIndex closed (see the header); false when it changed nothing
    method CloseLoop(const AIndex: int64): bool;
    var
      LBlocks: ref Int64List;
      LInstrs: ref Int64List;
      LChanged: bool;
      LI: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      if not DoShapeable(self.FFunction, self.FAnalysis, AIndex) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FIn := DoLoopSet(self.FAnalysis, self.FFunction.Blocks.Count, AIndex);
      if DoUnwindExit(self.FAnalysis, AIndex, self.FIn) then
        return false;
      end;
      if not self.DoExits(AIndex) then
        return false;
      end;
      LChanged := false;
      // The new phis go in blocks outside the loop: its blocks' lists stay as they are
      LBlocks := self.FAnalysis.LoopBlocks(AIndex);
      for LI := 0 to LBlocks.Count - 1 do
        LInstrs := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LBlocks[LI])).Instrs;
        for LK := 0 to LInstrs.Count - 1 do
          if self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LK]).ValueType = IRType.Void then
            skip;
          end;
          if self.DoCloseValue(LInstrs[LK]) then
            LChanged := true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LChanged;
    end;
  end;

// Every loop of AModule's function AFunction (its facts AAnalysis) closed, innermost
// first, the facts made again after a loop that changed (an outer loop then sees the phis
// an inner one made); true when any changed
func DoCloseLoops(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
  const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis): bool;
var
  LAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis;
  LCloser: ref LoopCloser;
  LChanged: bool;
  LD: int64;
  LL: int64;
begin
  LAnalysis := AAnalysis;
  LChanged := false;
  // Closing adds phis, never blocks: the loops keep their numbers in each new analysis
  for LD := DoMaxDepth(AAnalysis) downto 1 do
    for LL := 0 to LAnalysis.LoopCount() - 1 do
      if LAnalysis.LoopDepth(LL) <> LD then
        skip;
      end;
      LCloser := ref LoopCloser(AModule, AFunction, LAnalysis);
      if LCloser.CloseLoop(LL) then
        LChanged := true;
        LAnalysis := ref FunctionAnalysis(AModule, AFunction,
          ADAM_OPT_FACTS_LOOPS | ADAM_OPT_FACTS_USES);
      end;
    end;
  end;
  return LChanged;
end;

// AModule's function AFunction (its facts AAnalysis) with every loop it can shape in the
// loop form (see the header): preheader, one latch, dedicated exits, lcssa; true when it
// changed the function. Every loop pass calls it first
public func FormLoops(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
  const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis): bool;
var
  LAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis;
  LChanged: bool;
  LSteps: int64;
  LLimit: int64;
begin
  if AAnalysis.LoopCount() = 0 then
    return false;
  end;
  LAnalysis := AAnalysis;
  LChanged := false;
  LSteps := 0;
  // Each step adds one block that settles an edge set for good: more steps than this is
  // a compiler bug (a step that does not settle)
  LLimit := 4 * AModule.FunctionAt(AFunction).Blocks.Count + 16;
  while DoShapeStep(AModule, AFunction, LAnalysis) do
    LChanged := true;
    LSteps := LSteps + 1;
    if LSteps > LLimit then
      raise(ADAM_LOOPS_FAULT_UNSETTLED + IntToStr(AFunction));
    end;
    LAnalysis := ref FunctionAnalysis(AModule, AFunction,
      ADAM_OPT_FACTS_LOOPS | ADAM_OPT_FACTS_USES);
  end;
  if DoCloseLoops(AModule, AFunction, LAnalysis) then
    LChanged := true;
  end;
  return LChanged;
end;

// True for the ops licm moves when their operands are invariant (see the header)
func DoPure(const AKind: IROp): bool;
begin
  return (AKind = IROp.Constant) or (AKind = IROp.Add) or (AKind = IROp.Sub) or
    (AKind = IROp.Mul) or (AKind = IROp.BitAnd) or (AKind = IROp.BitOr) or
    (AKind = IROp.BitXor) or (AKind = IROp.Neg) or (AKind = IROp.BitNot) or
    (AKind = IROp.Shl) or (AKind = IROp.Shr) or (AKind = IROp.Sar) or
    (AKind = IROp.SDiv) or (AKind = IROp.UDiv) or (AKind = IROp.SRem) or
    (AKind = IROp.URem) or (AKind = IROp.FDiv) or (AKind = IROp.Compare) or
    (AKind = IROp.Offset) or (AKind = IROp.Convert) or (AKind = IROp.Address) or
    (AKind = IROp.CodeAddress) or (AKind = IROp.ImportAddress) or
    (AKind = IROp.ThreadAddress) or IsBitOp(AKind);
end;

// True for the ops that may write memory a load reads
func DoWrites(const AKind: IROp): bool;
begin
  return (AKind = IROp.Store) or (AKind = IROp.Copy) or (AKind = IROp.Fill) or
    (AKind = IROp.Call) or (AKind = IROp.CallExternal) or (AKind = IROp.CallIndirect) or
    IsAtomicOp(AKind);
end;

// True for the calls (each may write any memory but a slot whose address stays in its
// loads and stores)
func DoIsCall(const AKind: IROp): bool;
begin
  return (AKind = IROp.Call) or (AKind = IROp.CallExternal) or (AKind = IROp.CallIndirect);
end;

// What a base of the kind AKind is (ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_*)
func DoBaseClass(const AKind: IROp): int64;
begin
  if AKind = IROp.Slot then
    return ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_SLOT;
  end;
  if AKind = IROp.Address then
    return ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_DATA;
  end;
  if AKind = IROp.ThreadAddress then
    return ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_THREAD;
  end;
  return ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_OTHER;
end;

// True when the byte ranges at AOffset (ASize bytes) and AOther (AOtherSize) off one base
// may overlap: false only when both offsets are known, both sizes known and they are apart
func DoOverlap(const AOffset: int64; const AKnown: bool; const ASize: int64;
  const AOther: int64; const AOtherKnown: bool; const AOtherSize: int64): bool;
begin
  if (not AKnown) or (not AOtherKnown) or (ASize < 0) or (AOtherSize < 0) then
    return true;
  end;
  return not ((AOffset + ASize <= AOther) or (AOther + AOtherSize <= AOffset));
end;

type
  // licm over one function (see the header)
  InvariantHoister = object
    hidden FModule: ref IRModule;
    hidden FFunction: ref IRFunction;
    hidden FFunctionId: int64;
    hidden FAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis;
    // Each slot's escape mark, made when first asked (missing: not yet)
    hidden FSlotFacts: ref Int64Map;
    // The loop being hoisted from: its blocks, its preheader (a block id), the
    // instructions moved there (in order), those of the loop that may write memory,
    // whether a load may move (no scope resumes in the loop) and whether the loop holds a
    // call (a threadaddr stays in it then, G1d0)
    hidden FIn: BoolArray;
    hidden FPreheader: int64;
    hidden FMoved: ref Int64List;
    hidden FWriters: ref Int64List;
    hidden FLoadsMove: bool;
    hidden FLoopCalls: bool;
    // The module's routine facts (a pure call that moves, DoMoves)
    hidden FRoutines: ref RoutineFacts;

    // licm over AModule's function AFunction, its facts AAnalysis (blocks and edges it
    // never changes)
    init(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
      const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis);
    begin
      self.FModule := AModule;
      self.FFunction := AModule.FunctionAt(AFunction);
      self.FFunctionId := AFunction;
      self.FAnalysis := AAnalysis;
      self.FSlotFacts := ref Int64Map(ADAM_LOOPS_NONE);
      self.FPreheader := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FMoved := ref Int64List();
      self.FWriters := ref Int64List();
      self.FLoadsMove := false;
      self.FLoopCalls := false;
      self.FRoutines := ref RoutineFacts(AModule);
    end;

    // True when the value AId is made outside the loop (a funclet's parent slot too) or
    // has moved out already
    hidden const method DoInvariant(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(self.FModule.InstrAt(AId).Block);
      if LAt < 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      return not self.FIn[LAt];
    end;

    // True when every operand of AInstr is invariant
    hidden const method DoOperandsInvariant(const AInstr: ref IRInstr): bool;
    var
      LE: int64;
    begin
      for LE := 0 to AInstr.Operands.Count - 1 do
        if not self.DoInvariant(AInstr.Operands[LE]) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The slot ASlot's escape mark (ADAM_LOOPS_KEPT / ESCAPED / FUNCLET): whether its
    // address, or one moved from it, is ever used but as a load's, store's, copy's or
    // fill's place, or by a funclet
    hidden method DoSlotFact(const ASlot: int64): int64;
    var
      LWork: ref Int64List;
      LUses: ref Int64List;
      LUser: ref IRInstr;
      LFact: int64;
      LPointer: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LFact := self.FSlotFacts.Find(ASlot);
      if LFact <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
        return LFact;
      end;
      LFact := ADAM_LOOPS_KEPT;
      LWork := ref Int64List();
      LWork.Add(ASlot);
      while (LWork.Count > 0) and (LFact <> ADAM_LOOPS_FUNCLET) do
        LPointer := LWork.RemoveLast();
        LUses := self.FAnalysis.UsesOf(LPointer);
        for LI := 0 to LUses.Count - 1 do
          LUser := self.FModule.InstrAt(LUses[LI]);
          if self.FModule.BlockAt(LUser.Block).Owner <> self.FFunctionId then
            LFact := ADAM_LOOPS_FUNCLET;
            leave;
          end;
          if (LUser.Kind = IROp.Load) or (LUser.Kind = IROp.Copy) or
            (LUser.Kind = IROp.Fill) then
            skip;
          end;
          if (LUser.Kind = IROp.Store) and (LUser.Operands[1] <> LPointer) then
            skip;
          end;
          if (LUser.Kind = IROp.Offset) and (LUser.Operands[1] <> LPointer) then
            LWork.Add(LUses[LI]);
            skip;
          end;
          LFact := ADAM_LOOPS_ESCAPED;
        end;
      end;
      self.FSlotFacts.Put(ASlot, LFact);
      return LFact;
    end;

    // The base AAddress is moved from by Offsets (ABase), the bytes they move it by
    // (AOffset) and whether every step is a constant (AKnown)
    hidden const method DoBase(const AAddress: int64; var ABase: int64; var AOffset: int64;
      var AKnown: bool);
    var
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
      LStep: ref IRInstr;
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := AAddress;
      AOffset := 0;
      AKnown := true;
      LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LAt);
      while LInstr.Kind = IROp.Offset do
        LStep := self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[1]);
        if LStep.Kind = IROp.Constant then
          AOffset := AOffset + LStep.Imm;
        else
          AKnown := false;
        end;
        LAt := LInstr.Operands[0];
        LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LAt);
      end;
      ABase := LAt;
    end;

    // True when the ASize bytes at AAddress and the AOtherSize bytes at AOther may overlap
    // (see the header)
    hidden method DoMayAlias(const AAddress: int64; const ASize: int64; const AOther: int64;
      const AOtherSize: int64): bool;
    var
      LBase: ref IRInstr;
      LOtherBase: ref IRInstr;
      LKnown: bool;
      LOtherKnown: bool;
      LBaseId: int64;
      LOtherId: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LOtherOffset: int64;
      LClass: int64;
      LOtherClass: int64;
    begin
      self.DoBase(AAddress, LBaseId, LOffset, LKnown);
      self.DoBase(AOther, LOtherId, LOtherOffset, LOtherKnown);
      if LBaseId = LOtherId then
        return DoOverlap(LOffset, LKnown, ASize, LOtherOffset, LOtherKnown, AOtherSize);
      end;
      LBase := self.FModule.InstrAt(LBaseId);
      LOtherBase := self.FModule.InstrAt(LOtherId);
      LClass := DoBaseClass(LBase.Kind);
      LOtherClass := DoBaseClass(LOtherBase.Kind);
      if (LClass <> ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_OTHER) and (LOtherClass <> ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_OTHER) then
        if (LClass <> LOtherClass) or (LClass = ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_SLOT) then
          return false;
        end;
        // Two data / threadstatic addresses are one blob when they name one symbol
        if self.FModule.DataAt(LBase.Link).Symbol <>
          self.FModule.DataAt(LOtherBase.Link).Symbol then
          return false;
        end;
        return DoOverlap(LOffset, LKnown, ASize, LOtherOffset, LOtherKnown, AOtherSize);
      end;
      // An unknown pointer reaches anything but a slot whose address stays in its accesses
      if LClass = ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_SLOT then
        return self.DoSlotFact(LBaseId) <> ADAM_LOOPS_KEPT;
      end;
      if LOtherClass = ADAM_LOOPS_BASE_SLOT then
        return self.DoSlotFact(LOtherId) <> ADAM_LOOPS_KEPT;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // True when a writer of the loop may write what the load ALoad reads
    hidden method DoWrittenInLoop(const ALoad: ref IRInstr): bool;
    var
      LWriter: ref IRInstr;
      LBase: ref IRInstr;
      LKnown: bool;
      LBaseId: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LLoadSize: int64;
      LAddress: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LAddress := ALoad.Operands[0];
      LLoadSize := IRTypeWidth(ALoad.ValueType) div 8;
      for LI := 0 to self.FWriters.Count - 1 do
        LWriter := self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FWriters[LI]);
        if DoIsCall(LWriter.Kind) then
          self.DoBase(LAddress, LBaseId, LOffset, LKnown);
          LBase := self.FModule.InstrAt(LBaseId);
          if (LBase.Kind <> IROp.Slot) or (self.DoSlotFact(LBaseId) <> ADAM_LOOPS_KEPT) then
            return true;
          end;
          skip;
        end;
        if IsAtomicOp(LWriter.Kind) then
          // An atomic's place: bytes not counted
          LSize := ADAM_LOOPS_ANY_SIZE;
          if self.DoMayAlias(LAddress, LLoadSize,
            LWriter.Operands[0], LSize) then
            return true;
          end;
          skip;
        end;
        if LWriter.Kind = IROp.Store then
          LSize := IRTypeWidth(self.FModule.InstrAt(LWriter.Operands[1]).ValueType) div 8;
        else
          // A copy's or a fill's destination, Imm bytes
          LSize := LWriter.Imm;
        end;
        if self.DoMayAlias(LAddress, LLoadSize,
          LWriter.Operands[0], LSize) then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // True when the address AId is known valid: a slot's, a data blob's or a
    // threadstatic's, or one of them moved by a constant (Adam.Opt.DCE's rule)
    hidden const method DoValidAddress(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
    begin
      LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(AId);
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Offset then
        if self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[1]).Kind <> IROp.Constant then
          return false;
        end;
        LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[0]);
      end;
      return (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Slot) or (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Address) or
        (LInstr.Kind = IROp.ThreadAddress);
    end;

    // True when AInstr may fault: a load whose address is not known valid, a division by
    // anything but a constant known not to (Adam.Opt.DCE's rule)
    hidden const method DoMayFault(const AInstr: ref IRInstr): bool;
    var
      LDivisor: ref IRInstr;
      LSigned: bool;
    begin
      if AInstr.Kind = IROp.Load then
        return not self.DoValidAddress(AInstr.Operands[0]);
      end;
      LSigned := (AInstr.Kind = IROp.SDiv) or (AInstr.Kind = IROp.SRem);
      if (not LSigned) and (AInstr.Kind <> IROp.UDiv) and (AInstr.Kind <> IROp.URem) then
        return false;
      end;
      LDivisor := self.FModule.InstrAt(AInstr.Operands[1]);
      if (LDivisor.Kind <> IROp.Constant) or (LDivisor.Imm = 0) then
        return true;
      end;
      // A constant's Imm is canonical (sign-extended for a signed type): a signed -1 is -1
      return LSigned and (LDivisor.Imm = -1);
    end;

    // True when AInstr moves to the preheader (see the header); AClean: it is in the
    // header with nothing ahead of it there that has a side effect or may fault
    hidden method DoMoves(const AInstr: ref IRInstr; const AClean: bool): bool;
    var
      LKnown: bool;
      LBase: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
    begin
      if AInstr.Kind = IROp.Load then
        if (not self.FLoadsMove) or (not self.DoInvariant(AInstr.Operands[0])) then
          return false;
        end;
        self.DoBase(AInstr.Operands[0], LBase, LOffset, LKnown);
        if (self.FModule.InstrAt(LBase).Kind = IROp.Slot) and
          (self.DoSlotFact(LBase) = ADAM_LOOPS_FUNCLET) then
          return false;
        end;
        if self.DoWrittenInLoop(AInstr) then
          return false;
        end;
      else
        // a call of a pure routine that ends quietly (Adam.Opt.Facts) moves as a pure op:
        // it reads no memory the loop writes and cannot fault
        if AInstr.Kind = IROp.Call then
          if not (self.FRoutines.IsPure(AInstr.Link) and
            self.FRoutines.IsNoThrow(AInstr.Link)) then
            return false;
          end;
          if not self.DoOperandsInvariant(AInstr) then
            return false;
          end;
          return true;
        end;
        // a thread's own copy's address stays in a loop holding a call (see the header)
        if (AInstr.Kind = IROp.ThreadAddress) and self.FLoopCalls then
          return false;
        end;
        if (not DoPure(AInstr.Kind)) or (not self.DoOperandsInvariant(AInstr)) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      if self.DoMayFault(AInstr) then
        return AClean;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // licm over the loop AIndex (see the header); true when anything moved
    hidden method DoHoistLoop(const AIndex: int64): bool;
    var
      LBlocks: ref Int64List;
      LRpo: ref Int64List;
      LInstrs: ref Int64List;
      LKept: ref Int64List;
      LPlaced: ref Int64List;
      LBlock: ref IRBlock;
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
      LClean: bool;
      LHeader: int64;
      LPreheader: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      if not DoShapeable(self.FFunction, self.FAnalysis, AIndex) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FIn := DoLoopSet(self.FAnalysis, self.FFunction.Blocks.Count, AIndex);
      LPreheader := DoPreheaderOf(self.FModule, self.FFunction, self.FAnalysis, AIndex,
        self.FIn);
      if LPreheader = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
        return false;
      end;
      LHeader := self.FAnalysis.LoopHeader(AIndex);
      self.FPreheader := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LPreheader);
      self.FMoved := ref Int64List();
      self.FWriters := ref Int64List();
      self.FLoadsMove := true;
      self.FLoopCalls := false;
      LBlocks := self.FAnalysis.LoopBlocks(AIndex);
      for LI := 0 to LBlocks.Count - 1 do
        if DoIsResume(self.FFunction, LBlocks[LI]) then
          self.FLoadsMove := false;
        end;
        LInstrs := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LBlocks[LI])).Instrs;
        for LK := 0 to LInstrs.Count - 1 do
          if DoWrites(self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LK]).Kind) then
            self.FWriters.Add(LInstrs[LK]);
          end;
          if DoIsCall(self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LK]).Kind) then
            self.FLoopCalls := true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      // In reverse postorder an operand's block comes before its users' (it dominates
      // them), so an operand moves before its users are judged
      LRpo := self.FAnalysis.Rpo();
      for LI := 0 to LRpo.Count - 1 do
        LAt := LRpo[LI];
        if not self.FIn[LAt] then
          skip;
        end;
        LBlock := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LAt));
        LClean := LAt = LHeader;
        LKept := ref Int64List();
        for LK := 0 to LBlock.Instrs.Count - 1 do
          LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LBlock.Instrs[LK]);
          if self.DoMoves(LInstr, LClean) then
            LInstr.Block := self.FPreheader;
            self.FMoved.Add(LBlock.Instrs[LK]);
          else
            LKept.Add(LBlock.Instrs[LK]);
            if DoWrites(LInstr.Kind) or self.DoMayFault(LInstr) then
              LClean := false;
            end;
          end;
        end;
        if LKept.Count <> LBlock.Instrs.Count then
          LBlock.Instrs := LKept;
        end;
      end;
      if self.FMoved.Count = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      // The preheader: its own code, the moved instructions in order, its jump
      LBlock := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FPreheader);
      LPlaced := ref Int64List();
      for LK := 0 to LBlock.Instrs.Count - 2 do
        LPlaced.Add(LBlock.Instrs[LK]);
      end;
      for LK := 0 to self.FMoved.Count - 1 do
        LPlaced.Add(self.FMoved[LK]);
      end;
      LPlaced.Add(LBlock.Instrs[LBlock.Instrs.Count - 1]);
      LBlock.Instrs := LPlaced;
      return true;
    end;

    // licm over every loop, innermost first (what an inner loop moves out its outer loop
    // judges next); true when anything moved
    method Run(): bool;
    var
      LChanged: bool;
      LD: int64;
      LL: int64;
    begin
      LChanged := false;
      for LD := DoMaxDepth(self.FAnalysis) downto 1 do
        for LL := 0 to self.FAnalysis.LoopCount() - 1 do
          if self.FAnalysis.LoopDepth(LL) <> LD then
            skip;
          end;
          if self.DoHoistLoop(LL) then
            LChanged := true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LChanged;
    end;
  end;

// The pass licm (see the header) over AModule's function AFunction with its analysis
// AAnalysis: the loop form first (FormLoops), then the invariants moved out; true when it
// changed the function
public func HoistInvariants(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
  const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis): bool;
var
  LAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis;
  LHoister: ref InvariantHoister;
  LChanged: bool;
begin
  if AAnalysis.LoopCount() = 0 then
    return false;
  end;
  LChanged := FormLoops(AModule, AFunction, AAnalysis);
  LAnalysis := AAnalysis;
  if LChanged then
    LAnalysis := ref FunctionAnalysis(AModule, AFunction,
      ADAM_OPT_FACTS_LOOPS | ADAM_OPT_FACTS_USES);
  end;
  LHoister := ref InvariantHoister(AModule, AFunction, LAnalysis);
  if LHoister.Run() then
    LChanged := true;
  end;
  return LChanged;
end;

// True when AValue is within ACap of zero (either side)
func DoWithin(const AValue: int64; const ACap: int64): bool;
begin
  return (AValue <= ACap) and (AValue >= -ACap);
end;

// The lesser and the greater of two values
func DoLesser(const AValue: int64; const AOther: int64): int64;
begin
  if AOther < AValue then
    return AOther;
  end;
  return AValue;
end;

func DoGreater(const AValue: int64; const AOther: int64): int64;
begin
  if AOther > AValue then
    return AOther;
  end;
  return AValue;
end;

// The lowest value of the integer type AType, held to the range cap
func DoTypeLow(const AType: IRType): int64;
var
  LWidth: int64;
begin
  if not IsSignedType(AType) then
    return 0;
  end;
  LWidth := IRTypeWidth(AType);
  if LWidth >= 64 then
    return -ADAM_LOOPS_RANGE_CAP;
  end;
  return -int64(uint64(1) shl uint64(LWidth - 1));
end;

// The highest value of the integer type AType, held to the range cap
func DoTypeHigh(const AType: IRType): int64;
var
  LWidth: int64;
begin
  LWidth := IRTypeWidth(AType);
  if IsSignedType(AType) then
    if LWidth >= 64 then
      return ADAM_LOOPS_RANGE_CAP;
    end;
    return int64(uint64(1) shl uint64(LWidth - 1)) - 1;
  end;
  if LWidth >= 63 then
    return ADAM_LOOPS_RANGE_CAP;
  end;
  return int64(uint64(1) shl uint64(LWidth)) - 1;
end;

// The value of the integer constant AInstr (its canonical Imm read at its type) in AValue;
// false for anything else or a value past the range cap (an unsigned one above 2^63 reads
// negative)
func DoConstantValue(const AInstr: ref IRInstr; var AValue: int64): bool;
begin
  if (AInstr.Kind <> IROp.Constant) or (not IsIntegerType(AInstr.ValueType)) then
    return false;
  end;
  if (not IsSignedType(AInstr.ValueType)) and (AInstr.Imm < 0) then
    return false;
  end;
  if not DoWithin(AInstr.Imm, ADAM_LOOPS_RANGE_CAP) then
    return false;
  end;
  AValue := AInstr.Imm;
  return true;
end;

// The signed step an add (or a sub when ASub) of the constant AImm makes on a value of the
// integer type AType: a narrow unsigned constant's top half steps down; 0 when it is past
// the affine cap (no induction variable)
func DoSignedStride(const AType: IRType; const AImm: int64; const ASub: bool): int64;
var
  LStride: int64;
  LWidth: int64;
begin
  if not DoWithin(AImm, ADAM_LOOPS_RANGE_CAP) then
    return 0;
  end;
  LStride := AImm;
  LWidth := IRTypeWidth(AType);
  if (not IsSignedType(AType)) and (LWidth < 64) then
    if LStride >= int64(uint64(1) shl uint64(LWidth - 1)) then
      LStride := LStride - int64(uint64(1) shl uint64(LWidth));
    end;
  end;
  if ASub then
    LStride := -LStride;
  end;
  if not DoWithin(LStride, ADAM_LOOPS_AFFINE_CAP) then
    return 0;
  end;
  return LStride;
end;

// The predicate that holds of B and A when APredicate holds of A and B (operands swapped)
func DoSwapped(const APredicate: IRPredicate): IRPredicate;
begin
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SLess then
    return IRPredicate.SGreater;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SLessEqual then
    return IRPredicate.SGreaterEqual;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SGreater then
    return IRPredicate.SLess;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SGreaterEqual then
    return IRPredicate.SLessEqual;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.ULess then
    return IRPredicate.UGreater;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.ULessEqual then
    return IRPredicate.UGreaterEqual;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.UGreater then
    return IRPredicate.ULess;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.UGreaterEqual then
    return IRPredicate.ULessEqual;
  end;
  return APredicate;
end;

// The integer predicate that holds exactly when APredicate does not (equal and the orders;
// any other is given back as it is: indvars reads only integer compares)
func DoNegated(const APredicate: IRPredicate): IRPredicate;
begin
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.Equal then
    return IRPredicate.NotEqual;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.NotEqual then
    return IRPredicate.Equal;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SLess then
    return IRPredicate.SGreaterEqual;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SLessEqual then
    return IRPredicate.SGreater;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SGreater then
    return IRPredicate.SLessEqual;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SGreaterEqual then
    return IRPredicate.SLess;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.ULess then
    return IRPredicate.UGreaterEqual;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.ULessEqual then
    return IRPredicate.UGreater;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.UGreater then
    return IRPredicate.ULessEqual;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.UGreaterEqual then
    return IRPredicate.ULess;
  end;
  return APredicate;
end;

// True when the ranges ALow..AHigh (the left operand) and AOtherLow..AOtherHigh (the
// right) decide the integer compare APredicate, its value in AValue (an unsigned order is
// read as the signed one: the caller passes ranges of values that are not negative)
func DoDecide(const APredicate: IRPredicate; const ALow: int64; const AHigh: int64;
  const AOtherLow: int64; const AOtherHigh: int64; var AValue: bool): bool;
var
  LSame: bool;
  LApart: bool;
begin
  if (APredicate = IRPredicate.SLess) or (APredicate = IRPredicate.ULess) then
    if AHigh < AOtherLow then
      AValue := true;
      return true;
    end;
    if ALow >= AOtherHigh then
      AValue := false;
      return true;
    end;
    return false;
  end;
  if (APredicate = IRPredicate.SLessEqual) or (APredicate = IRPredicate.ULessEqual) then
    if AHigh <= AOtherLow then
      AValue := true;
      return true;
    end;
    if ALow > AOtherHigh then
      AValue := false;
      return true;
    end;
    return false;
  end;
  if (APredicate = IRPredicate.SGreater) or (APredicate = IRPredicate.UGreater) then
    if ALow > AOtherHigh then
      AValue := true;
      return true;
    end;
    if AHigh <= AOtherLow then
      AValue := false;
      return true;
    end;
    return false;
  end;
  if (APredicate = IRPredicate.SGreaterEqual) or (APredicate = IRPredicate.UGreaterEqual) then
    if ALow >= AOtherHigh then
      AValue := true;
      return true;
    end;
    if AHigh < AOtherLow then
      AValue := false;
      return true;
    end;
    return false;
  end;
  if (APredicate <> IRPredicate.Equal) and (APredicate <> IRPredicate.NotEqual) then
    return false;
  end;
  LSame := (ALow = AHigh) and (AOtherLow = AOtherHigh) and (ALow = AOtherLow);
  LApart := (AHigh < AOtherLow) or (AOtherHigh < ALow);
  if (not LSame) and (not LApart) then
    return false;
  end;
  // Equal holds when both are the one same value, not when they are apart
  AValue := LSame;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.NotEqual then
    AValue := not LSame;
  end;
  return true;
end;

type
  // What indvars knows of one basic induction variable of the loop it works on (see the
  // header)
  InductionFact = record
    // The header phi, its value from the preheader and its signed step a turn
    PhiId: int64;
    Seed: int64;
    Stride: int64;
    // Its exit test (a loop block's position, ADAM_LOOPS_NONE: none found), the block the
    // edge staying in the loop runs to (a position) and the value it is compared with
    TestAt: int64;
    StayAt: int64;
    LimitValue: int64;
    // Its range in every block of the loop, and in the blocks the stay block dominates
    HasLoopRange: bool;
    LoopLow: int64;
    LoopHigh: int64;
    HasStayRange: bool;
    StayLow: int64;
    StayHigh: int64;
    // Its value on the test's exit edge (ADAM_LOOPS_EXIT_*): ExitValue is the value's id
    // or the constant
    ExitKind: int64;
    ExitValue: int64;
  end;

  InductionFactArray = array of InductionFact;

  // indvars over one function (see the header)
  InductionSimplifier = object
    hidden FModule: ref IRModule;
    hidden FFunction: ref IRFunction;
    hidden FFunctionId: int64;
    hidden FAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis;
    // The loop being worked: its number, its blocks, its header, preheader and latch (by
    // position), and its induction variables' facts
    hidden FLoop: int64;
    hidden FIn: BoolArray;
    hidden FHeader: int64;
    hidden FPreheader: int64;
    hidden FLatch: int64;
    hidden FFacts: InductionFactArray;
    hidden FFactCount: int64;
    // How many ranges the current DoRange walks took from an induction variable
    hidden FInductionHits: int64;

    // indvars over AModule's function AFunction, its facts AAnalysis (it never changes a
    // block or an edge, so the loops keep their numbers in every analysis made after)
    init(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
      const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis);
    begin
      self.FModule := AModule;
      self.FFunction := AModule.FunctionAt(AFunction);
      self.FFunctionId := AFunction;
      self.FAnalysis := AAnalysis;
      self.FLoop := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FHeader := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FPreheader := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FLatch := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FFactCount := 0;
      self.FInductionHits := 0;
    end;

    // True when the value AId is made in a block of the loop
    hidden const method DoInLoop(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(self.FModule.InstrAt(AId).Block);
      if LAt < 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      return self.FIn[LAt];
    end;

    // The fact whose phi is AId (ADAM_LOOPS_NONE: no induction variable of the loop)
    hidden const method DoFactOf(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LK: int64;
    begin
      for LK := 0 to self.FFactCount - 1 do
        if self.FFacts[LK].PhiId = AId then
          return LK;
        end;
      end;
      return ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
    end;

    // A new instruction (AKind, AType, ANode) in the block ABlock (an id), just before its
    // terminator; returns its id
    hidden method DoEmitBefore(const ABlock: int64; const AKind: IROp; const AType: IRType;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    begin
      return DoEmitAtEnd(self.FModule, ABlock, AKind, AType, ANode);
    end;

    // A new instruction AKind of AType over ALeft and ARight in the block ABlock (an id),
    // just before its terminator; returns its id
    hidden method DoBinaryBefore(const ABlock: int64; const AKind: IROp; const AType: IRType;
      const ALeft: int64; const ARight: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := self.DoEmitBefore(ABlock, AKind, AType, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ALeft);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ARight);
      return LId;
    end;

    // A convert of AValue to AType in the block ABlock (an id), just before its terminator
    hidden method DoConvertBefore(const ABlock: int64; const AType: IRType; const AValue: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := self.DoEmitBefore(ABlock, IROp.Convert, AType, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(AValue);
      return LId;
    end;

    // An add of ALeft and ARight (of AType) in the header, after its phis; returns its id
    hidden method DoAddAfterPhis(const AType: IRType; const ALeft: int64; const ARight: int64;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LBlock: ref IRBlock;
      LPlaced: ref Int64List;
      LPut: bool;
      LHeader: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LHeader := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FHeader);
      LId := self.FModule.Emit(LHeader, IROp.Add, AType, ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ALeft);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Operands.Add(ARight);
      // Emit put it last: the list made again with it at the first instruction no phi
      LBlock := self.FModule.BlockAt(LHeader);
      LCount := LBlock.Instrs.Count;
      LPlaced := ref Int64List();
      LPut := false;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 2 do
        if (not LPut) and (self.FModule.InstrAt(LBlock.Instrs[LI]).Kind <> IROp.Phi) then
          LPlaced.Add(LId);
          LPut := true;
        end;
        LPlaced.Add(LBlock.Instrs[LI]);
      end;
      if not LPut then
        LPlaced.Add(LId);
      end;
      LBlock.Instrs := LPlaced;
      return LId;
    end;

    // A constant AValue of AType in the preheader (it dominates the loop and its exits),
    // at ANode; returns its id
    hidden method DoConstant(const AType: IRType; const AValue: int64; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      LId := self.DoEmitBefore(self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FPreheader), IROp.Constant, AType,
        ANode);
      self.FModule.InstrAt(LId).Imm := IRCanonicalImm(AType, AValue);
      return LId;
    end;

    // Every use of the value AOld made AValue (its users from the analysis: a use a pass
    // step made since is kept, still the same value)
    hidden method DoReplaceUses(const AOld: int64; const AValue: int64);
    var
      LUses: ref Int64List;
      LUser: ref IRInstr;
      LI: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      LUses := self.FAnalysis.UsesOf(AOld);
      for LI := 0 to LUses.Count - 1 do
        LUser := self.FModule.InstrAt(LUses[LI]);
        for LE := 0 to LUser.Operands.Count - 1 do
          if LUser.Operands[LE] = AOld then
            LUser.Operands[LE] := AValue;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The fact AIndex's loop-wide range ALow..AHigh (none when it is empty)
    hidden method DoLoopRange(const AIndex: int64; const ALow: int64; const AHigh: int64);
    begin
      if ALow > AHigh then
        return;
      end;
      self.FFacts[AIndex].HasLoopRange := true;
      self.FFacts[AIndex].LoopLow := ALow;
      self.FFacts[AIndex].LoopHigh := AHigh;
    end;

    // The fact AIndex's range ALow..AHigh where its test held (none when it is empty)
    hidden method DoStayRange(const AIndex: int64; const ALow: int64; const AHigh: int64);
    begin
      if ALow > AHigh then
        return;
      end;
      self.FFacts[AIndex].HasStayRange := true;
      self.FFacts[AIndex].StayLow := ALow;
      self.FFacts[AIndex].StayHigh := AHigh;
    end;

    // The fact AIndex's value on its test's exit edge: the constant AValue
    hidden method DoExitConstant(const AIndex: int64; const AValue: int64);
    begin
      self.FFacts[AIndex].ExitKind := ADAM_LOOPS_EXIT_CONSTANT;
      self.FFacts[AIndex].ExitValue := AValue;
    end;

    // The fact AIndex's ranges and exit value from its test, which stays in the loop while
    // `variable APredicate limit` holds (see the header). Each range holds by induction:
    // the variable starts inside it and the latch, reached only through the stay edge,
    // steps it from a value the test let through to one still inside, never wrapping
    hidden method DoSetRanges(const AIndex: int64; const APredicate: IRPredicate);
    var
      LType: IRType;
      LSeed: int64;
      LLimit: int64;
      LStride: int64;
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[AIndex].PhiId).ValueType;
      LStride := self.FFacts[AIndex].Stride;
      // A not-equal test lets the loop go only when the variable is its limit
      if APredicate = IRPredicate.NotEqual then
        self.FFacts[AIndex].ExitKind := ADAM_LOOPS_EXIT_VALUE;
        self.FFacts[AIndex].ExitValue := self.FFacts[AIndex].LimitValue;
      end;
      if not DoConstantValue(self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[AIndex].Seed), LSeed) then
        return;
      end;
      if not DoConstantValue(self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[AIndex].LimitValue), LLimit) then
        return;
      end;
      LLow := DoTypeLow(LType);
      LHigh := DoTypeHigh(LType);
      if APredicate = IRPredicate.NotEqual then
        // By one toward the limit from a start not past it: it meets the limit
        if (LStride = 1) and (LSeed <= LLimit) then
          self.DoLoopRange(AIndex, LSeed, LLimit);
          self.DoStayRange(AIndex, LSeed, LLimit - 1);
        end;
        if (LStride = -1) and (LSeed >= LLimit) then
          self.DoLoopRange(AIndex, LLimit, LSeed);
          self.DoStayRange(AIndex, LLimit + 1, LSeed);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      // A less / greater test: every range needs the step from the last value the test
      // lets through to stay inside the type (else it wraps past the start)
      if (LStride > 0) and
        ((APredicate = IRPredicate.SLess) or (APredicate = IRPredicate.ULess)) then
        if LLimit - 1 + LStride <= LHigh then
          self.DoStayRange(AIndex, LSeed, LLimit - 1);
          self.DoLoopRange(AIndex, LSeed, DoGreater(LSeed, LLimit - 1 + LStride));
          if (LStride = 1) and (LSeed <= LLimit) then
            self.DoExitConstant(AIndex, LLimit);
          end;
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if (LStride > 0) and
        ((APredicate = IRPredicate.SLessEqual) or (APredicate = IRPredicate.ULessEqual)) then
        if LLimit + LStride <= LHigh then
          self.DoStayRange(AIndex, LSeed, LLimit);
          self.DoLoopRange(AIndex, LSeed, DoGreater(LSeed, LLimit + LStride));
          if (LStride = 1) and (LSeed <= LLimit + 1) then
            self.DoExitConstant(AIndex, LLimit + 1);
          end;
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if (LStride < 0) and
        ((APredicate = IRPredicate.SGreater) or (APredicate = IRPredicate.UGreater)) then
        if LLimit + 1 + LStride >= LLow then
          self.DoStayRange(AIndex, LLimit + 1, LSeed);
          self.DoLoopRange(AIndex, DoLesser(LSeed, LLimit + 1 + LStride), LSeed);
          if (LStride = -1) and (LSeed >= LLimit) then
            self.DoExitConstant(AIndex, LLimit);
          end;
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if (LStride < 0) and
        ((APredicate = IRPredicate.SGreaterEqual) or (APredicate = IRPredicate.UGreaterEqual)) then
        if LLimit + LStride >= LLow then
          self.DoStayRange(AIndex, LLimit, LSeed);
          self.DoLoopRange(AIndex, DoLesser(LSeed, LLimit + LStride), LSeed);
          if (LStride = -1) and (LSeed >= LLimit - 1) then
            self.DoExitConstant(AIndex, LLimit - 1);
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The exit test of the fact AIndex (see the header): the first loop block, by position,
    // whose branch compares the phi with an invariant and has one edge in the loop, that
    // edge's block entered from it alone and dominating the latch
    hidden method DoFindTest(const AIndex: int64);
    var
      LBlocks: ref Int64List;
      LPreds: ref Int64List;
      LTerm: ref IRInstr;
      LCondition: ref IRInstr;
      LPhi: ref IRInstr;
      LPredicate: IRPredicate;
      LOther: int64;
      LThen: int64;
      LElse: int64;
      LStay: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LPhi := self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[AIndex].PhiId);
      LBlocks := self.FAnalysis.LoopBlocks(self.FLoop);
      for LI := 0 to LBlocks.Count - 1 do
        LAt := LBlocks[LI];
        LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(self.FModule, self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LAt));
        if LTerm.Kind <> IROp.Branch then
          skip;
        end;
        LCondition := self.FModule.InstrAt(LTerm.Operands[0]);
        if LCondition.Kind <> IROp.Compare then
          skip;
        end;
        // Read as `phi LPredicate other`
        if LCondition.Operands[0] = self.FFacts[AIndex].PhiId then
          LOther := LCondition.Operands[1];
          LPredicate := LCondition.Predicate;
        else
          if LCondition.Operands[1] <> self.FFacts[AIndex].PhiId then
            skip;
          end;
          LOther := LCondition.Operands[0];
          LPredicate := DoSwapped(LCondition.Predicate);
        end;
        if self.DoInLoop(LOther) and (self.FModule.InstrAt(LOther).Kind <> IROp.Constant) then
          skip;
        end;
        if IsSignedPredicate(LPredicate) and (not IsSignedType(LPhi.ValueType)) then
          skip;
        end;
        if IsUnsignedPredicate(LPredicate) and IsSignedType(LPhi.ValueType) then
          skip;
        end;
        LThen := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(LTerm.Targets[0]);
        LElse := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(LTerm.Targets[1]);
        if (LThen < 0) or (LElse < 0) then
          skip;
        end;
        if self.FIn[LThen] = self.FIn[LElse] then
          skip;
        end;
        // Read as the test that keeps the loop going
        if self.FIn[LThen] then
          LStay := LThen;
        else
          LStay := LElse;
          LPredicate := DoNegated(LPredicate);
        end;
        LPreds := self.FAnalysis.PredsOf(LStay);
        if (LPreds.Count <> 1) or (LPreds[0] <> LAt) then
          skip;
        end;
        if not self.FAnalysis.Dominates(LStay, self.FLatch) then
          skip;
        end;
        self.FFacts[AIndex].TestAt := LAt;
        self.FFacts[AIndex].StayAt := LStay;
        self.FFacts[AIndex].LimitValue := LOther;
        self.DoSetRanges(AIndex, LPredicate);
        return;
      end;
    end;

    // The loop's basic induction variables (see the header), each with its exit test
    hidden method DoFindInductions();
    var
      LHeader: ref IRBlock;
      LPhi: ref IRInstr;
      LNext: ref IRInstr;
      LPreheader: int64;
      LLatch: int64;
      LPhiId: int64;
      LSeed: int64;
      LNextId: int64;
      LStride: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      self.FFactCount := 0;
      setlength(self.FFacts, 0);
      LHeader := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FHeader));
      LPreheader := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FPreheader);
      LLatch := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FLatch);
      for LK := 0 to LHeader.Instrs.Count - 1 do
        LPhiId := LHeader.Instrs[LK];
        LPhi := self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhiId);
        if LPhi.Kind <> IROp.Phi then
          leave;
        end;
        if (not IsIntegerType(LPhi.ValueType)) or (LPhi.Operands.Count <> 2) then
          skip;
        end;
        LSeed := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
        LNextId := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
        for LE := 0 to 1 do
          if LPhi.Targets[LE] = LPreheader then
            LSeed := LPhi.Operands[LE];
          end;
          if LPhi.Targets[LE] = LLatch then
            LNextId := LPhi.Operands[LE];
          end;
        end;
        if (LSeed = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE) or (LNextId = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE) then
          skip;
        end;
        // The latch's value: the phi plus or less a constant
        LNext := self.FModule.InstrAt(LNextId);
        LStride := 0;
        if (LNext.Kind = IROp.Add) or (LNext.Kind = IROp.Sub) then
          if (LNext.Operands[0] = LPhiId) and
            (self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext.Operands[1]).Kind = IROp.Constant) then
            LStride := DoSignedStride(LPhi.ValueType, self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext.Operands[1]).Imm,
              LNext.Kind = IROp.Sub);
          end;
          if (LNext.Kind = IROp.Add) and (LNext.Operands[1] = LPhiId) and
            (self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext.Operands[0]).Kind = IROp.Constant) then
            LStride := DoSignedStride(LPhi.ValueType, self.FModule.InstrAt(LNext.Operands[0]).Imm,
              false);
          end;
        end;
        if LStride = 0 then
          skip;
        end;
        LAt := self.FFactCount;
        setlength(self.FFacts, LAt + 1);
        self.FFacts[LAt].PhiId := LPhiId;
        self.FFacts[LAt].Seed := LSeed;
        self.FFacts[LAt].Stride := LStride;
        self.FFacts[LAt].TestAt := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
        self.FFacts[LAt].StayAt := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
        self.FFacts[LAt].LimitValue := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
        self.FFacts[LAt].HasLoopRange := false;
        self.FFacts[LAt].LoopLow := 0;
        self.FFacts[LAt].LoopHigh := 0;
        self.FFacts[LAt].HasStayRange := false;
        self.FFacts[LAt].StayLow := 0;
        self.FFacts[LAt].StayHigh := 0;
        self.FFacts[LAt].ExitKind := ADAM_LOOPS_EXIT_NONE;
        self.FFacts[LAt].ExitValue := 0;
        self.FFactCount := LAt + 1;
        self.DoFindTest(LAt);
      end;
    end;

    // ALow..AHigh (ALowIn..AHighIn) when it is inside the integer type AType's values (the
    // value computed never wrapped)
    hidden const method DoKeep(const AType: IRType; const ALowIn: int64; const AHighIn: int64;
      var ALow: int64; var AHigh: int64): bool;
    begin
      if (ALowIn < DoTypeLow(AType)) or (AHighIn > DoTypeHigh(AType)) then
        return false;
      end;
      ALow := ALowIn;
      AHigh := AHighIn;
      return true;
    end;

    // The range of the value AId in the loop block at AAt (see the header's checks) in
    // ALow..AHigh; false when it is not known
    hidden method DoRange(const AId: int64; const AAt: int64; const ADepth: int64;
      var ALow: int64; var AHigh: int64): bool;
    var
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
      LTerm: int64;
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LOtherLow: int64;
      LOtherHigh: int64;
      LFactor: int64;
      LFact: int64;
    begin
      if ADepth > ADAM_LOOPS_WALK_DEPTH then
        return false;
      end;
      LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(AId);
      if not IsIntegerType(LInstr.ValueType) then
        return false;
      end;
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Constant then
        if not DoConstantValue(LInstr, LLow) then
          return false;
        end;
        ALow := LLow;
        AHigh := LLow;
        return true;
      end;
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Phi then
        LFact := self.DoFactOf(AId);
        if LFact = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
          return false;
        end;
        if self.FFacts[LFact].HasStayRange and
          self.FAnalysis.Dominates(self.FFacts[LFact].StayAt, AAt) then
          ALow := self.FFacts[LFact].StayLow;
          AHigh := self.FFacts[LFact].StayHigh;
          self.FInductionHits := self.FInductionHits + 1;
          return true;
        end;
        if self.FFacts[LFact].HasLoopRange and self.FIn[AAt] then
          ALow := self.FFacts[LFact].LoopLow;
          AHigh := self.FFacts[LFact].LoopHigh;
          self.FInductionHits := self.FInductionHits + 1;
          return true;
        end;
        return false;
      end;
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Convert then
        if not IsIntegerType(self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[0]).ValueType) then
          return false;
        end;
        if not self.DoRange(LInstr.Operands[0], AAt, ADepth + 1, LLow, LHigh) then
          return false;
        end;
        // An integer that fits its new type keeps its value
        return self.DoKeep(LInstr.ValueType, LLow, LHigh, ALow, AHigh);
      end;
      if (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Add) or (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Sub) then
        if not self.DoRange(LInstr.Operands[0], AAt, ADepth + 1, LLow, LHigh) then
          return false;
        end;
        if not self.DoRange(LInstr.Operands[1], AAt, ADepth + 1, LOtherLow, LOtherHigh) then
          return false;
        end;
        // Every end is within 2^62: no sum or difference overflows
        if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Add then
          return self.DoKeep(LInstr.ValueType, LLow + LOtherLow, LHigh + LOtherHigh, ALow,
            AHigh);
        end;
        return self.DoKeep(LInstr.ValueType, LLow - LOtherHigh, LHigh - LOtherLow, ALow, AHigh);
      end;
      if (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Mul) or (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Shl) then
        // A multiply by a constant on either side, a shift by a constant count
        if DoConstantValue(self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[1]), LFactor) then
          LTerm := LInstr.Operands[0];
        else
          if (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Shl) or
            (not DoConstantValue(self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[0]), LFactor)) then
            return false;
          end;
          LTerm := LInstr.Operands[1];
        end;
        if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Shl then
          if (LFactor < 0) or (LFactor > ADAM_LOOPS_MAX_SHIFT) then
            return false;
          end;
          LFactor := int64(uint64(1) shl uint64(LFactor));
        end;
        if not DoWithin(LFactor, ADAM_LOOPS_AFFINE_CAP) then
          return false;
        end;
        if not self.DoRange(LTerm, AAt, ADepth + 1, LLow, LHigh) then
          return false;
        end;
        if (not DoWithin(LLow, ADAM_LOOPS_PRODUCT_CAP)) or
          (not DoWithin(LHigh, ADAM_LOOPS_PRODUCT_CAP)) then
          return false;
        end;
        if LFactor < 0 then
          return self.DoKeep(LInstr.ValueType, LHigh * LFactor, LLow * LFactor, ALow, AHigh);
        end;
        return self.DoKeep(LInstr.ValueType, LLow * LFactor, LHigh * LFactor, ALow, AHigh);
      end;
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.BitAnd then
        // An and with a constant that is not negative is between 0 and that constant
        if DoConstantValue(self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[1]), LFactor) or
          DoConstantValue(self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[0]), LFactor) then
          if LFactor >= 0 then
            return self.DoKeep(LInstr.ValueType, 0, LFactor, ALow, AHigh);
          end;
        end;
        return false;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // checks (see the header): true when a branch of the loop got a constant
    hidden method DoFoldChecks(): bool;
    var
      LBlocks: ref Int64List;
      LTerm: ref IRInstr;
      LCondition: ref IRInstr;
      LTruth: bool;
      LChanged: bool;
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LOtherLow: int64;
      LOtherHigh: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LConstant: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LChanged := false;
      LBlocks := self.FAnalysis.LoopBlocks(self.FLoop);
      for LI := 0 to LBlocks.Count - 1 do
        LAt := LBlocks[LI];
        LBlock := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LAt);
        LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(self.FModule, LBlock);
        if LTerm.Kind <> IROp.Branch then
          skip;
        end;
        LCondition := self.FModule.InstrAt(LTerm.Operands[0]);
        if LCondition.Kind <> IROp.Compare then
          skip;
        end;
        if not IsIntegerType(self.FModule.InstrAt(LCondition.Operands[0]).ValueType) then
          skip;
        end;
        // Only a compare an induction variable's range decides (sccp has the rest)
        self.FInductionHits := 0;
        if not self.DoRange(LCondition.Operands[0], LAt, 0, LLow, LHigh) then
          skip;
        end;
        if not self.DoRange(LCondition.Operands[1], LAt, 0, LOtherLow, LOtherHigh) then
          skip;
        end;
        if self.FInductionHits = 0 then
          skip;
        end;
        if IsUnsignedPredicate(LCondition.Predicate) and ((LLow < 0) or (LOtherLow < 0)) then
          skip;
        end;
        if not DoDecide(LCondition.Predicate, LLow, LHigh, LOtherLow, LOtherHigh, LTruth) then
          skip;
        end;
        // The branch reads a bool constant (0 / 1) instead: simplifycfg folds it
        LConstant := self.DoEmitBefore(LBlock, IROp.Constant, IRType.Bool, LCondition.Node);
        if LTruth then
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LConstant).Imm := 1;
        else
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LConstant).Imm := 0;
        end;
        LTerm.Operands[0] := LConstant;
        LChanged := true;
      end;
      return LChanged;
    end;

    // exits (see the header): true when an exit phi took a variable's exit value
    hidden method DoExitValues(): bool;
    var
      LTerm: ref IRInstr;
      LExit: ref IRBlock;
      LPhi: ref IRInstr;
      LChanged: bool;
      LTest: int64;
      LExitId: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      LChanged := false;
      for LK := 0 to self.FFactCount - 1 do
        if self.FFacts[LK].ExitKind = ADAM_LOOPS_EXIT_NONE then
          skip;
        end;
        LTest := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FFacts[LK].TestAt);
        LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(self.FModule, LTest);
        LExitId := LTerm.Targets[0];
        if self.FIn[self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(LExitId)] then
          LExitId := LTerm.Targets[1];
        end;
        LExit := self.FModule.BlockAt(LExitId);
        LValue := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
        for LI := 0 to LExit.Instrs.Count - 1 do
          LPhi := self.FModule.InstrAt(LExit.Instrs[LI]);
          if LPhi.Kind <> IROp.Phi then
            leave;
          end;
          for LE := 0 to LPhi.Targets.Count - 1 do
            if (LPhi.Targets[LE] <> LTest) or (LPhi.Operands[LE] <> self.FFacts[LK].PhiId) then
              skip;
            end;
            if LValue = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
              if self.FFacts[LK].ExitKind = ADAM_LOOPS_EXIT_VALUE then
                LValue := self.FFacts[LK].ExitValue;
              else
                LValue := self.DoConstant(self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[LK].PhiId).ValueType,
                  self.FFacts[LK].ExitValue, LPhi.Node);
              end;
            end;
            LPhi.Operands[LE] := LValue;
            LChanged := true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LChanged;
    end;

    // The value AId as AScale * variable + AOffset over the fact AFact (ADAM_LOOPS_NONE:
    // no variable, a constant), at 64 bits (see the header's reduction); AMultiplies set
    // when a multiply or a shift was read. False when it is no such count
    hidden method DoAffine(const AId: int64; const ADepth: int64; var AFact: int64;
      var AScale: int64; var AOffset: int64; var AMultiplies: bool): bool;
    var
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
      LSource: ref IRInstr;
      LTerm: int64;
      LFact: int64;
      LScale: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LOtherFact: int64;
      LOtherScale: int64;
      LOtherOffset: int64;
      LFactor: int64;
      LValue: int64;
    begin
      if ADepth > ADAM_LOOPS_WALK_DEPTH then
        return false;
      end;
      LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(AId);
      if (not IsIntegerType(LInstr.ValueType)) or (IRTypeWidth(LInstr.ValueType) <> 64) then
        return false;
      end;
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Constant then
        if not DoConstantValue(LInstr, LValue) then
          return false;
        end;
        if not DoWithin(LValue, ADAM_LOOPS_AFFINE_CAP) then
          return false;
        end;
        AFact := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
        AScale := 0;
        AOffset := LValue;
        return true;
      end;
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Phi then
        LFact := self.DoFactOf(AId);
        if LFact = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
          return false;
        end;
        AFact := LFact;
        AScale := 1;
        AOffset := 0;
        return true;
      end;
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Convert then
        LSource := self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[0]);
        if not IsIntegerType(LSource.ValueType) then
          return false;
        end;
        if IRTypeWidth(LSource.ValueType) = 64 then
          // int64 and uint64 are the same bits
          return self.DoAffine(LInstr.Operands[0], ADepth + 1, AFact, AScale, AOffset,
            AMultiplies);
        end;
        // A narrower variable widened: its own value while it stays in its range (it
        // never wraps) and the widening keeps its sign
        if LSource.Kind <> IROp.Phi then
          return false;
        end;
        LFact := self.DoFactOf(LInstr.Operands[0]);
        if LFact = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
          return false;
        end;
        if not self.FFacts[LFact].HasLoopRange then
          return false;
        end;
        if IsSignedType(LSource.ValueType) and (not IsSignedType(LInstr.ValueType)) and
          (self.FFacts[LFact].LoopLow < 0) then
          return false;
        end;
        AFact := LFact;
        AScale := 1;
        AOffset := 0;
        return true;
      end;
      if (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Add) or (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Sub) then
        if not self.DoAffine(LInstr.Operands[0], ADepth + 1, LFact, LScale, LOffset,
          AMultiplies) then
          return false;
        end;
        if not self.DoAffine(LInstr.Operands[1], ADepth + 1, LOtherFact, LOtherScale,
          LOtherOffset, AMultiplies) then
          return false;
        end;
        if (LFact <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE) and (LOtherFact <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE) and
          (LFact <> LOtherFact) then
          return false;
        end;
        if LFact = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
          LFact := LOtherFact;
        end;
        if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Sub then
          LOtherScale := -LOtherScale;
          LOtherOffset := -LOtherOffset;
        end;
        AFact := LFact;
        AScale := LScale + LOtherScale;
        AOffset := LOffset + LOtherOffset;
        return DoWithin(AScale, ADAM_LOOPS_AFFINE_CAP) and
          DoWithin(AOffset, ADAM_LOOPS_AFFINE_CAP);
      end;
      if (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Mul) or (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Shl) then
        if DoConstantValue(self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[1]), LFactor) then
          LTerm := LInstr.Operands[0];
        else
          if (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Shl) or
            (not DoConstantValue(self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[0]), LFactor)) then
            return false;
          end;
          LTerm := LInstr.Operands[1];
        end;
        if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Shl then
          if (LFactor < 0) or (LFactor > ADAM_LOOPS_MAX_SHIFT) then
            return false;
          end;
          LFactor := int64(uint64(1) shl uint64(LFactor));
        end;
        if not DoWithin(LFactor, ADAM_LOOPS_AFFINE_CAP) then
          return false;
        end;
        if not self.DoAffine(LTerm, ADepth + 1, LFact, LScale, LOffset, AMultiplies) then
          return false;
        end;
        // Both within 2^30: no product overflows
        AFact := LFact;
        AScale := LScale * LFactor;
        AOffset := LOffset * LFactor;
        AMultiplies := true;
        return DoWithin(AScale, ADAM_LOOPS_AFFINE_CAP) and
          DoWithin(AOffset, ADAM_LOOPS_AFFINE_CAP);
      end;
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Neg then
        if not self.DoAffine(LInstr.Operands[0], ADepth + 1, LFact, LScale, LOffset,
          AMultiplies) then
          return false;
        end;
        AFact := LFact;
        AScale := -LScale;
        AOffset := -LOffset;
        return true;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // reduction (see the header): true when an address became a pointer phi
    hidden method DoReduce(): bool;
    var
      LBlocks: ref Int64List;
      LCurrent: ref Int64List;
      LInstrs: ref Int64List;
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
      LSeed: ref IRInstr;
      LMultiplies: bool;
      LFact: int64;
      LScale: int64;
      LOffset: int64;
      LSeedValue: int64;
      LFactor: int64;
      LBytes: int64;
      LStart: int64;
      LStep: int64;
      LPhi: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LPreheader: int64;
      LLatch: int64;
      LHeader: int64;
      LNode: int64;
      LReduced: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      LReduced := 0;
      LPreheader := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FPreheader);
      LLatch := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FLatch);
      LHeader := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FHeader);
      LBlocks := self.FAnalysis.LoopBlocks(self.FLoop);
      for LI := 0 to LBlocks.Count - 1 do
        // The block's instructions as they are now (the header and the latch get new ones)
        LCurrent := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LBlocks[LI])).Instrs;
        LInstrs := ref Int64List();
        for LK := 0 to LCurrent.Count - 1 do
          LInstrs.Add(LCurrent[LK]);
        end;
        for LK := 0 to LInstrs.Count - 1 do
          LId := LInstrs[LK];
          LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LId);
          if LInstr.Kind <> IROp.Offset then
            skip;
          end;
          if self.DoInLoop(LInstr.Operands[0]) then
            skip;
          end;
          LFact := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
          LScale := 0;
          LOffset := 0;
          LMultiplies := false;
          if not self.DoAffine(LInstr.Operands[1], 0, LFact, LScale, LOffset, LMultiplies) then
            skip;
          end;
          if (LFact = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE) or (LScale = 0) or (not LMultiplies) then
            skip;
          end;
          LNode := LInstr.Node;
          LSeed := self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[LFact].Seed);
          // The first turn's count: folded from a known start, else made in the preheader
          if DoConstantValue(LSeed, LSeedValue) and
            DoWithin(LSeedValue, ADAM_LOOPS_PRODUCT_CAP) then
            LBytes := self.DoConstant(IRType.Int64, LScale * LSeedValue + LOffset, LNode);
          else
            // A narrower variable has a constant start (its range is known)
            if IRTypeWidth(LSeed.ValueType) <> 64 then
              skip;
            end;
            LBytes := self.FFacts[LFact].Seed;
            if LSeed.ValueType <> IRType.Int64 then
              LBytes := self.DoConvertBefore(LPreheader, IRType.Int64, LBytes, LNode);
            end;
            if LScale <> 1 then
              LFactor := self.DoConstant(IRType.Int64, LScale, LNode);
              LBytes := self.DoBinaryBefore(LPreheader, IROp.Mul, IRType.Int64, LBytes, LFactor,
                LNode);
            end;
            if LOffset <> 0 then
              LFactor := self.DoConstant(IRType.Int64, LOffset, LNode);
              LBytes := self.DoBinaryBefore(LPreheader, IROp.Add, IRType.Int64, LBytes, LFactor,
                LNode);
            end;
          end;
          LStart := self.DoBinaryBefore(LPreheader, IROp.Offset, IRType.Pointer,
            LInstr.Operands[0], LBytes, LNode);
          // Each turn moves it by the scale times the stride (both within 2^30)
          LStep := self.DoConstant(IRType.Int64, LScale * self.FFacts[LFact].Stride, LNode);
          LPhi := DoNewPhi(self.FModule, LHeader, IRType.Pointer, LNode);
          LNext := self.DoBinaryBefore(LLatch, IROp.Offset, IRType.Pointer, LPhi, LStep, LNode);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Operands.Add(LStart);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Targets.Add(LPreheader);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Operands.Add(LNext);
          self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhi).Targets.Add(LLatch);
          self.DoReplaceUses(LId, LPhi);
          LReduced := LReduced + 1;
          if LReduced >= ADAM_LOOPS_MAX_REDUCED then
            return true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LReduced > 0;
    end;

    // The variable the fact AIndex merges into (see the header's merging): the first of
    // its type and stride with an exit test, else the first of them (AIndex itself: kept)
    hidden const method DoKeptInduction(const AIndex: int64): int64;
    var
      LType: IRType;
      LFirst: int64;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      LType := self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[AIndex].PhiId).ValueType;
      LFirst := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      for LJ := 0 to self.FFactCount - 1 do
        if (self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[LJ].PhiId).ValueType <> LType) or
          (self.FFacts[LJ].Stride <> self.FFacts[AIndex].Stride) then
          skip;
        end;
        if self.FFacts[LJ].TestAt <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
          return LJ;
        end;
        if LFirst = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
          LFirst := LJ;
        end;
      end;
      return LFirst;
    end;

    // merging (see the header): true when a variable became another plus a difference
    hidden method DoMergeInductions(): bool;
    var
      LPhi: ref IRInstr;
      LType: IRType;
      LChanged: bool;
      LKeep: int64;
      LSeed: int64;
      LOtherSeed: int64;
      LDelta: int64;
      LValue: int64;
      LPreheader: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      LChanged := false;
      LPreheader := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FPreheader);
      for LK := 0 to self.FFactCount - 1 do
        LKeep := self.DoKeptInduction(LK);
        if LKeep = LK then
          skip;
        end;
        LPhi := self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[LK].PhiId);
        LType := LPhi.ValueType;
        if DoConstantValue(self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[LK].Seed), LOtherSeed) and
          DoConstantValue(self.FModule.InstrAt(self.FFacts[LKeep].Seed), LSeed) and
          DoWithin(LOtherSeed, ADAM_LOOPS_PRODUCT_CAP) and
          DoWithin(LSeed, ADAM_LOOPS_PRODUCT_CAP) then
          if LOtherSeed = LSeed then
            LValue := self.FFacts[LKeep].PhiId;
          else
            LDelta := self.DoConstant(LType, LOtherSeed - LSeed, LPhi.Node);
            LValue := self.DoAddAfterPhis(LType, self.FFacts[LKeep].PhiId, LDelta, LPhi.Node);
          end;
        else
          LDelta := self.DoBinaryBefore(LPreheader, IROp.Sub, LType, self.FFacts[LK].Seed,
            self.FFacts[LKeep].Seed, LPhi.Node);
          LValue := self.DoAddAfterPhis(LType, self.FFacts[LKeep].PhiId, LDelta, LPhi.Node);
        end;
        self.DoReplaceUses(self.FFacts[LK].PhiId, LValue);
        LChanged := true;
      end;
      return LChanged;
    end;

    // indvars over the loop AIndex (see the header); true when it changed anything
    hidden method DoSimplifyLoop(const AIndex: int64): bool;
    var
      LPreds: ref Int64List;
      LChanged: bool;
      LLatch: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if not DoShapeable(self.FFunction, self.FAnalysis, AIndex) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FLoop := AIndex;
      self.FIn := DoLoopSet(self.FAnalysis, self.FFunction.Blocks.Count, AIndex);
      self.FPreheader := DoPreheaderOf(self.FModule, self.FFunction, self.FAnalysis, AIndex,
        self.FIn);
      if self.FPreheader = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FHeader := self.FAnalysis.LoopHeader(AIndex);
      // One latch: the header's one predecessor in the loop
      LPreds := self.FAnalysis.PredsOf(self.FHeader);
      LLatch := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      for LI := 0 to LPreds.Count - 1 do
        if self.FIn[LPreds[LI]] then
          if LLatch <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
            return false;
          end;
          LLatch := LPreds[LI];
        end;
      end;
      if LLatch = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FLatch := LLatch;
      self.DoFindInductions();
      if self.FFactCount = 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      // In this order, all from the one analysis: the checks and exits read the ranges
      // before merging changes the variables' uses
      LChanged := false;
      if self.DoFoldChecks() then
        LChanged := true;
      end;
      if self.DoExitValues() then
        LChanged := true;
      end;
      if self.DoReduce() then
        LChanged := true;
      end;
      if self.DoMergeInductions() then
        LChanged := true;
      end;
      return LChanged;
    end;

    // indvars over every loop, innermost first, the facts made again after a loop that
    // changed (its use lists); true when anything changed
    method Run(): bool;
    var
      LChanged: bool;
      LD: int64;
      LL: int64;
    begin
      LChanged := false;
      for LD := DoMaxDepth(self.FAnalysis) downto 1 do
        for LL := 0 to self.FAnalysis.LoopCount() - 1 do
          if self.FAnalysis.LoopDepth(LL) <> LD then
            skip;
          end;
          if self.DoSimplifyLoop(LL) then
            LChanged := true;
            self.FAnalysis := ref FunctionAnalysis(self.FModule, self.FFunctionId,
              ADAM_OPT_FACTS_LOOPS | ADAM_OPT_FACTS_USES);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LChanged;
    end;
  end;

// The pass indvars (see the header) over AModule's function AFunction with its analysis
// AAnalysis: the loop form first (FormLoops), then each loop's induction variables
// simplified; true when it changed the function
public func SimplifyInductions(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
  const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis): bool;
var
  LAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis;
  LSimplifier: ref InductionSimplifier;
  LChanged: bool;
begin
  if AAnalysis.LoopCount() = 0 then
    return false;
  end;
  LChanged := FormLoops(AModule, AFunction, AAnalysis);
  LAnalysis := AAnalysis;
  if LChanged then
    LAnalysis := ref FunctionAnalysis(AModule, AFunction,
      ADAM_OPT_FACTS_LOOPS | ADAM_OPT_FACTS_USES);
  end;
  LSimplifier := ref InductionSimplifier(AModule, AFunction, LAnalysis);
  if LSimplifier.Run() then
    LChanged := true;
  end;
  return LChanged;
end;

// The value AMap gives AValue; AValue itself when it gives none (a value from outside
// what was copied)
func DoMappedOf(const AMap: ref Int64Map; const AValue: int64): int64;
var
  LMapped: int64;
begin
  LMapped := AMap.Find(AValue);
  if LMapped = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
    return AValue;
  end;
  return LMapped;
end;

// The terminator of the block ABlock (an id) made to go to ATo wherever it went to AFrom
func DoRetarget(const AModule: ref IRModule; const ABlock: int64; const AFrom: int64;
  const ATo: int64);
var
  LTerm: ref IRInstr;
  LE: int64;
begin
  LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(AModule, ABlock);
  for LE := 0 to LTerm.Targets.Count - 1 do
    if LTerm.Targets[LE] = AFrom then
      LTerm.Targets[LE] := ATo;
    end;
  end;
end;

// The compare APredicate (no float one) of the constants ALeft and ARight of AType, as
// the machine compares them: each read at the type's width, signed for a signed predicate
func DoComparedAs(const APredicate: IRPredicate; const AType: IRType; const ALeft: int64;
  const ARight: int64): bool;
var
  LWidth: int64;
  LSignedLeft: int64;
  LSignedRight: int64;
  LLeft: uint64;
  LRight: uint64;
begin
  LWidth := IRTypeWidth(AType);
  LSignedLeft := ReadLowBits(ALeft, LWidth, true);
  LSignedRight := ReadLowBits(ARight, LWidth, true);
  LLeft := uint64(ReadLowBits(ALeft, LWidth, false));
  LRight := uint64(ReadLowBits(ARight, LWidth, false));
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.Equal then
    return LLeft = LRight;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.NotEqual then
    return LLeft <> LRight;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SLess then
    return LSignedLeft < LSignedRight;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SLessEqual then
    return LSignedLeft <= LSignedRight;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SGreater then
    return LSignedLeft > LSignedRight;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.SGreaterEqual then
    return LSignedLeft >= LSignedRight;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.ULess then
    return LLeft < LRight;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.ULessEqual then
    return LLeft <= LRight;
  end;
  if APredicate = IRPredicate.UGreater then
    return LLeft > LRight;
  end;
  return LLeft >= LRight;
end;

type
  // loopshape over one function (see the header)
  LoopShaper = object
    hidden FModule: ref IRModule;
    hidden FFunction: ref IRFunction;
    hidden FFunctionId: int64;
    hidden FAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis;
    // The headers (block ids) each shape has tried, and how many shapes the function took
    hidden FUnswitched: ref Int64List;
    hidden FUnrolled: ref Int64List;
    hidden FRotated: ref Int64List;
    hidden FShapes: int64;
    // The loop being worked (DoTake): its blocks (a mark per position, and the positions),
    // its header, preheader and latch (positions, and ids: a shape's new blocks move the
    // positions, never the ids) and how many instructions it has
    hidden FIn: BoolArray;
    hidden FBlocks: ref Int64List;
    hidden FHeader: int64;
    hidden FPreheader: int64;
    hidden FLatch: int64;
    hidden FHeaderId: int64;
    hidden FPreheaderId: int64;
    hidden FLatchId: int64;
    hidden FSize: int64;

    // loopshape over AModule's function AFunction, its facts AAnalysis (its loops in form)
    init(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
      const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis);
    begin
      self.FModule := AModule;
      self.FFunction := AModule.FunctionAt(AFunction);
      self.FFunctionId := AFunction;
      self.FAnalysis := AAnalysis;
      self.FUnswitched := ref Int64List();
      self.FUnrolled := ref Int64List();
      self.FRotated := ref Int64List();
      self.FShapes := 0;
      self.FBlocks := ref Int64List();
      self.FHeader := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FPreheader := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FLatch := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FHeaderId := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FPreheaderId := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FLatchId := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      self.FSize := 0;
    end;

    // True when the value AId is made in a block of the loop (read before a shape edits)
    hidden const method DoInLoop(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(self.FModule.InstrAt(AId).Block);
      if LAt < 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      return self.FIn[LAt];
    end;

    // True when every operand of the phi APhi that is AId arrives from a block of the loop
    hidden const method DoFromLoop(const APhi: ref IRInstr; const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      for LE := 0 to APhi.Operands.Count - 1 do
        if APhi.Operands[LE] <> AId then
          skip;
        end;
        LAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(APhi.Targets[LE]);
        if (LAt < 0) or (not self.FIn[LAt]) then
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The loop AIndex taken as the one worked when a shape can copy it (see the header):
    // shapeable, with a preheader and one latch, innermost, every block reached, no
    // resume block, no unwind edge out, no slot / parameter / varargs start in it, every
    // block ending in a jump or a branch, every value it makes closed (a use outside it is
    // an exit phi's operand from a loop block)
    hidden method DoTake(const AIndex: int64): bool;
    var
      LBlock: ref IRBlock;
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
      LUser: ref IRInstr;
      LPreds: ref Int64List;
      LUses: ref Int64List;
      LAt: int64;
      LUserAt: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      if not DoShapeable(self.FFunction, self.FAnalysis, AIndex) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FIn := DoLoopSet(self.FAnalysis, self.FFunction.Blocks.Count, AIndex);
      self.FBlocks := self.FAnalysis.LoopBlocks(AIndex);
      self.FHeader := self.FAnalysis.LoopHeader(AIndex);
      self.FPreheader := DoPreheaderOf(self.FModule, self.FFunction, self.FAnalysis, AIndex,
        self.FIn);
      if self.FPreheader = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
        return false;
      end;
      // One latch: the header's one predecessor in the loop
      LPreds := self.FAnalysis.PredsOf(self.FHeader);
      LCount := 0;
      for LI := 0 to LPreds.Count - 1 do
        if self.FIn[LPreds[LI]] then
          LCount := LCount + 1;
          self.FLatch := LPreds[LI];
        end;
      end;
      if LCount <> 1 then
        return false;
      end;
      if DoUnwindExit(self.FAnalysis, AIndex, self.FIn) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.FSize := 0;
      for LI := 0 to self.FBlocks.Count - 1 do
        LAt := self.FBlocks[LI];
        if self.FAnalysis.LoopOf(LAt) <> AIndex then
          return false;
        end;
        if (not self.FAnalysis.Reachable(LAt)) or DoIsResume(self.FFunction, LAt) then
          return false;
        end;
        LBlock := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LAt));
        for LK := 0 to LBlock.Instrs.Count - 1 do
          LId := LBlock.Instrs[LK];
          LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LId);
          if (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Slot) or (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Parameter) or
            (LInstr.Kind = IROp.ChainParameter) or (LInstr.Kind = IROp.VarargsStart) then
            return false;
          end;
          if IsTerminator(LInstr.Kind) and (LInstr.Kind <> IROp.Jump) and
            (LInstr.Kind <> IROp.Branch) then
            return false;
          end;
          self.FSize := self.FSize + 1;
          LUses := self.FAnalysis.UsesOf(LId);
          for LE := 0 to LUses.Count - 1 do
            LUser := self.FModule.InstrAt(LUses[LE]);
            LUserAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(LUser.Block);
            if LUserAt < 0 then
              return false;
            end;
            if self.FIn[LUserAt] then
              skip;
            end;
            if (LUser.Kind <> IROp.Phi) or (not self.DoFromLoop(LUser, LId)) then
              return false;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      self.FHeaderId := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FHeader);
      self.FPreheaderId := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FPreheader);
      self.FLatchId := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FLatch);
      return true;
    end;

    // The blocks outside the loop its blocks' terminators go to (ids, each once); read
    // before a shape adds a block
    hidden const method DoExits(): ref Int64List;
    var
      LExits: ref Int64List;
      LTerm: ref IRInstr;
      LTarget: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      LExits := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to self.FBlocks.Count - 1 do
        LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(self.FModule, self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FBlocks[LI]));
        for LE := 0 to LTerm.Targets.Count - 1 do
          LTarget := LTerm.Targets[LE];
          LAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(LTarget);
          if (LAt >= 0) and self.FIn[LAt] then
            skip;
          end;
          if LExits.IndexOf(LTarget) < 0 then
            LExits.Add(LTarget);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LExits;
    end;

    // One copy of the loop: a new block beside each of its blocks (in that block's
    // scopes), each instruction copied with its operands and targets made the copy's (a
    // value or a block from outside the loop kept); ABlocks and AValues take each block's
    // and each value's id to its copy's. The exits' phis are the caller's (DoExitEntries)
    hidden method DoCloneLoop(const ABlocks: ref Int64Map; const AValues: ref Int64Map);
    var
      LIds: ref Int64List;
      LCopies: ref Int64List;
      LSource: ref IRBlock;
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
      LCopy: ref IRInstr;
      LOld: int64;
      LNew: int64;
      LCopyId: int64;
      LMapped: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      // The ids first: each new block moves the positions after it
      LIds := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to self.FBlocks.Count - 1 do
        LIds.Add(self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FBlocks[LI]));
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LIds.Count - 1 do
        LOld := LIds[LI];
        LNew := self.FModule.InsertBlock(self.FFunctionId,
          self.FFunction.Blocks.IndexOf(LOld), false);
        ABlocks.Put(LOld, LNew);
      end;
      // Every instruction copied as it is, then its operands and targets made the copy's
      // (a phi's operand may come from a block later in the loop)
      LCopies := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to LIds.Count - 1 do
        LSource := self.FModule.BlockAt(LIds[LI]);
        LNew := ABlocks.Find(LIds[LI]);
        for LK := 0 to LSource.Instrs.Count - 1 do
          LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LSource.Instrs[LK]);
          LCopyId := self.FModule.Emit(LNew, LInstr.Kind, LInstr.ValueType, LInstr.Node);
          LCopy := self.FModule.InstrAt(LCopyId);
          LCopy.CopyFieldsFrom(LInstr);
          for LE := 0 to LInstr.Operands.Count - 1 do
            LCopy.Operands.Add(LInstr.Operands[LE]);
          end;
          for LE := 0 to LInstr.Targets.Count - 1 do
            LCopy.Targets.Add(LInstr.Targets[LE]);
          end;
          AValues.Put(LSource.Instrs[LK], LCopyId);
          LCopies.Add(LCopyId);
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LCopies.Count - 1 do
        LCopy := self.FModule.InstrAt(LCopies[LI]);
        for LE := 0 to LCopy.Operands.Count - 1 do
          LMapped := AValues.Find(LCopy.Operands[LE]);
          if LMapped <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
            LCopy.Operands[LE] := LMapped;
          end;
        end;
        for LE := 0 to LCopy.Targets.Count - 1 do
          LMapped := ABlocks.Find(LCopy.Targets[LE]);
          if LMapped <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
            LCopy.Targets[LE] := LMapped;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The phis of the exits AExits (ids) given a copy's entries (ABlocks, AValues as
    // DoCloneLoop made them): an entry from a block of the loop gets one from that block's
    // copy, with the copy's value (a value from outside the loop kept)
    hidden method DoExitEntries(const AExits: ref Int64List; const ABlocks: ref Int64Map;
      const AValues: ref Int64Map);
    var
      LInstrs: ref Int64List;
      LPhi: ref IRInstr;
      LFrom: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to AExits.Count - 1 do
        LInstrs := self.FModule.BlockAt(AExits[LI]).Instrs;
        for LK := 0 to LInstrs.Count - 1 do
          LPhi := self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LK]);
          if LPhi.Kind <> IROp.Phi then
            skip;
          end;
          // Only the entries it had: one an earlier copy added comes from no original block
          LCount := LPhi.Operands.Count;
          for LE := 0 to LCount - 1 do
            LFrom := ABlocks.Find(LPhi.Targets[LE]);
            if LFrom = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
              skip;
            end;
            LPhi.Operands.Add(DoMappedOf(AValues, LPhi.Operands[LE]));
            LPhi.Targets.Add(LFrom);
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The phis of the block ABlock (an id) given an entry from AFrom for each one from the
    // header: the value AMap gives (a value from outside the header kept)
    hidden method DoHeaderEntries(const ABlock: int64; const AMap: ref Int64Map;
      const AFrom: int64);
    var
      LInstrs: ref Int64List;
      LPhi: ref IRInstr;
      LCount: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      LInstrs := self.FModule.BlockAt(ABlock).Instrs;
      for LK := 0 to LInstrs.Count - 1 do
        LPhi := self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LK]);
        if LPhi.Kind <> IROp.Phi then
          skip;
        end;
        LCount := LPhi.Operands.Count;
        for LE := 0 to LCount - 1 do
          if LPhi.Targets[LE] = self.FHeaderId then
            LPhi.Operands.Add(DoMappedOf(AMap, LPhi.Operands[LE]));
            LPhi.Targets.Add(AFrom);
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The branch ending the block ABlock (an id) made to read the bool constant ACondition
    // (simplifycfg folds it)
    hidden method DoSetCondition(const ABlock: int64; const ACondition: bool);
    var
      LTerm: ref IRInstr;
      LConstant: int64;
    begin
      LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(self.FModule, ABlock);
      LConstant := DoEmitAtEnd(self.FModule, ABlock, IROp.Constant, IRType.Bool, LTerm.Node);
      if ACondition then
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LConstant).Imm := 1;
      else
        self.FModule.InstrAt(LConstant).Imm := 0;
      end;
      LTerm.Operands[0] := LConstant;
    end;

    // The loop's body laid out ACopies times in a row (see the header): copy k's latch
    // runs into copy k + 1's header, the last one's back to the loop's header; a copy's
    // header phis take the one value the copy before gave on its back edge, the header's
    // the last copy's. With AKnown the branch ending the block AExiting (an id) reads
    // AConditions[k] in copy k
    hidden method DoUnroll(const ACopies: int64; const AKnown: bool; const AExiting: int64;
      const AConditions: BoolArray);
    var
      LExits: ref Int64List;
      LPhis: ref Int64List;
      LBacks: ref Int64List;
      LHeaderInstrs: ref Int64List;
      LBlocks: ref Int64Map;
      LValues: ref Int64Map;
      LLast: ref Int64Map;
      LPhi: ref IRInstr;
      LCopyPhi: ref IRInstr;
      LLastHeader: int64;
      LLastLatch: int64;
      LCopyHeader: int64;
      LFirstCopy: int64;
      LC: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      LExits := self.DoExits();
      // The header's phis and each one's value on the back edge
      LPhis := ref Int64List();
      LBacks := ref Int64List();
      LHeaderInstrs := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FHeaderId).Instrs;
      for LK := 0 to LHeaderInstrs.Count - 1 do
        LPhi := self.FModule.InstrAt(LHeaderInstrs[LK]);
        if LPhi.Kind <> IROp.Phi then
          skip;
        end;
        for LE := 0 to LPhi.Targets.Count - 1 do
          if LPhi.Targets[LE] = self.FLatchId then
            LPhis.Add(LHeaderInstrs[LK]);
            LBacks.Add(LPhi.Operands[LE]);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      LLastHeader := self.FHeaderId;
      LLastLatch := self.FLatchId;
      LFirstCopy := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      LLast := ref Int64Map(ADAM_LOOPS_NONE);
      for LC := 1 to ACopies - 1 do
        LBlocks := ref Int64Map(ADAM_LOOPS_NONE);
        LValues := ref Int64Map(ADAM_LOOPS_NONE);
        self.DoCloneLoop(LBlocks, LValues);
        self.DoExitEntries(LExits, LBlocks, LValues);
        LCopyHeader := LBlocks.Find(self.FHeaderId);
        // The copy before runs into this one. The loop's own latch is cloned again by every
        // later copy, so its back edge must still go to the header until the last copy is
        // made: it moves after this walk (a copy's latch is never cloned, it moves now)
        if LC = 1 then
          LFirstCopy := LCopyHeader;
        else
          DoRetarget(self.FModule, LLastLatch, LLastHeader, LCopyHeader);
        end;
        // This copy's header has one predecessor: each phi one entry, from it
        for LK := 0 to LPhis.Count - 1 do
          LCopyPhi := self.FModule.InstrAt(LValues.Find(LPhis[LK]));
          LCopyPhi.Operands := ref Int64List();
          LCopyPhi.Targets := ref Int64List();
          LCopyPhi.Operands.Add(DoMappedOf(LLast, LBacks[LK]));
          LCopyPhi.Targets.Add(LLastLatch);
        end;
        if AKnown then
          self.DoSetCondition(LBlocks.Find(AExiting), AConditions[LC]);
        end;
        LLastHeader := LCopyHeader;
        LLastLatch := LBlocks.Find(self.FLatchId);
        LLast := LValues;
      end;
      // The loop's own latch into the first copy, now that no copy is cloned from it
      if LFirstCopy <> ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
        DoRetarget(self.FModule, self.FLatchId, self.FHeaderId, LFirstCopy);
      end;
      // The last copy back to the header: its phis' back edge entry is that copy's
      DoRetarget(self.FModule, LLastLatch, LLastHeader, self.FHeaderId);
      for LK := 0 to LPhis.Count - 1 do
        LPhi := self.FModule.InstrAt(LPhis[LK]);
        for LE := 0 to LPhi.Targets.Count - 1 do
          if LPhi.Targets[LE] = self.FLatchId then
            LPhi.Operands[LE] := DoMappedOf(LLast, LBacks[LK]);
            LPhi.Targets[LE] := LLastLatch;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if AKnown then
        self.DoSetCondition(AExiting, AConditions[0]);
      end;
    end;

    // The value AId in the loop's turn ATurn (0: the first) into AValue: a constant, a
    // header phi (its preheader value in the first turn, else its back edge value in the
    // turn before), a one-value phi, an integer add or sub (wrapped at its type's width as
    // the machine does); false for any other value, a value from outside the loop that is
    // no constant, or a walk past ADAM_LOOPS_WALK_DEPTH steps in one turn
    hidden method DoTurnValue(const AId: int64; const ATurn: int64; const ADepth: int64;
      var AValue: int64): bool;
    var
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LSeed: int64;
      LBack: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      if ADepth > ADAM_LOOPS_WALK_DEPTH then
        return false;
      end;
      LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(AId);
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Constant then
        if not (IsIntegerType(LInstr.ValueType) or (LInstr.ValueType = IRType.Bool)) then
          return false;
        end;
        AValue := LInstr.Imm;
        return true;
      end;
      if not self.DoInLoop(AId) then
        return false;
      end;
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Phi then
        if LInstr.Block = self.FHeaderId then
          LSeed := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
          LBack := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
          for LE := 0 to LInstr.Targets.Count - 1 do
            if LInstr.Targets[LE] = self.FPreheaderId then
              LSeed := LInstr.Operands[LE];
            end;
            if LInstr.Targets[LE] = self.FLatchId then
              LBack := LInstr.Operands[LE];
            end;
          end;
          if (LSeed = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE) or (LBack = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE) then
            return false;
          end;
          if ATurn = 0 then
            return self.DoTurnValue(LSeed, 0, ADepth + 1, AValue);
          end;
          // The turn before, a walk of its own: the turns fall, so the walks end
          return self.DoTurnValue(LBack, ATurn - 1, 0, AValue);
        end;
        if LInstr.Operands.Count = 1 then
          return self.DoTurnValue(LInstr.Operands[0], ATurn, ADepth + 1, AValue);
        end;
        return false;
      end;
      if ((LInstr.Kind = IROp.Add) or (LInstr.Kind = IROp.Sub)) and
        IsIntegerType(LInstr.ValueType) then
        if not self.DoTurnValue(LInstr.Operands[0], ATurn, ADepth + 1, LLeft) then
          return false;
        end;
        if not self.DoTurnValue(LInstr.Operands[1], ATurn, ADepth + 1, LRight) then
          return false;
        end;
        // uint64 arithmetic wraps as the machine's does; the type's width then taken
        if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Sub then
          AValue := IRCanonicalImm(LInstr.ValueType, int64(uint64(LLeft) - uint64(LRight)));
        else
          AValue := IRCanonicalImm(LInstr.ValueType, int64(uint64(LLeft) + uint64(LRight)));
        end;
        return true;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // The bool AId in the loop's turn ATurn into AValue: a bool constant, or a compare (no
    // float one) of two integer or bool values DoTurnValue knows
    hidden method DoTurnCondition(const AId: int64; const ATurn: int64;
      var AValue: bool): bool;
    var
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
      LType: IRType;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
    begin
      LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(AId);
      if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Constant then
        AValue := LInstr.Imm <> 0;
        return true;
      end;
      if (LInstr.Kind <> IROp.Compare) or IsFloatPredicate(LInstr.Predicate) then
        return false;
      end;
      LType := self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstr.Operands[0]).ValueType;
      if not (IsIntegerType(LType) or (LType = IRType.Bool)) then
        return false;
      end;
      if not self.DoTurnValue(LInstr.Operands[0], ATurn, 0, LLeft) then
        return false;
      end;
      if not self.DoTurnValue(LInstr.Operands[1], ATurn, 0, LRight) then
        return false;
      end;
      AValue := DoComparedAs(LInstr.Predicate, LType, LLeft, LRight);
      return true;
    end;

    // The loop fully unrolled (see the header) when its one exiting block, passed every
    // turn, ends in a branch DoTurnCondition knows in every turn up to the one it leaves
    // in, within ADAM_LOOPS_FULL_TURNS turns and ADAM_LOOPS_FULL_BUDGET instructions
    hidden method DoFullUnroll(): bool;
    var
      LConditions: BoolArray;
      LTerm: ref IRInstr;
      LCondition: bool;
      LStayOnTrue: bool;
      LExiting: int64;
      LExitingId: int64;
      LTurns: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LE: int64;
      LT: int64;
    begin
      // The one edge out of the loop
      LCount := 0;
      LExiting := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      for LI := 0 to self.FBlocks.Count - 1 do
        LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(self.FModule, self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FBlocks[LI]));
        for LE := 0 to LTerm.Targets.Count - 1 do
          LAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(LTerm.Targets[LE]);
          if (LAt < 0) or (not self.FIn[LAt]) then
            LCount := LCount + 1;
            LExiting := self.FBlocks[LI];
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if LCount <> 1 then
        return false;
      end;
      // Every turn passes it: it dominates the latch
      if not self.FAnalysis.Dominates(LExiting, self.FLatch) then
        return false;
      end;
      LExitingId := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(LExiting);
      LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(self.FModule, LExitingId);
      if LTerm.Kind <> IROp.Branch then
        return false;
      end;
      LAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(LTerm.Targets[0]);
      LStayOnTrue := (LAt >= 0) and self.FIn[LAt];
      setlength(LConditions, ADAM_LOOPS_FULL_TURNS);
      LTurns := 0;
      for LT := 0 to ADAM_LOOPS_FULL_TURNS - 1 do
        if not self.DoTurnCondition(LTerm.Operands[0], LT, LCondition) then
          return false;
        end;
        LConditions[LT] := LCondition;
        if LCondition <> LStayOnTrue then
          LTurns := LT + 1;
          leave;
        end;
      end;
      if (LTurns = 0) or (LTurns * self.FSize > ADAM_LOOPS_FULL_BUDGET) then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoUnroll(LTurns, true, LExitingId, LConditions);
      return true;
    end;

    // The loop partially unrolled (see the header): as many copies as fit
    // ADAM_LOOPS_PARTIAL_BUDGET instructions, up to ADAM_LOOPS_PARTIAL_COPIES, each with
    // its own exit tests (exact for any trip count, no remainder loop); false below two
    hidden method DoPartialUnroll(): bool;
    var
      LNone: BoolArray;
      LCopies: int64;
    begin
      LCopies := ADAM_LOOPS_PARTIAL_COPIES;
      while (LCopies > 1) and (LCopies * self.FSize > ADAM_LOOPS_PARTIAL_BUDGET) do
        LCopies := LCopies - 1;
      end;
      if LCopies < 2 then
        return false;
      end;
      setlength(LNone, 0);
      self.DoUnroll(LCopies, false, ADAM_LOOPS_NONE, LNone);
      return true;
    end;

    // The loop rotated (see the header) when its header is a test: a branch with one edge
    // to a stay block entered from it alone and one out of the loop, the header not the
    // latch, at most ADAM_LOOPS_ROTATE_SIZE instructions; ARotated takes the stay block
    // (an id), the new loop's header
    hidden method DoRotate(var ARotated: int64): bool;
    var
      LInstrs: ref Int64List;
      LValues: ref Int64List;
      LUses: ref Int64List;
      LOperands: ref Int64List;
      LTargets: ref Int64List;
      LMap: ref Int64Map;
      LTerm: ref IRInstr;
      LInstr: ref IRInstr;
      LCopy: ref IRInstr;
      LUser: ref IRInstr;
      LMergePhi: ref IRInstr;
      LStay: int64;
      LExit: int64;
      LStayAt: int64;
      LExitAt: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LCopyId: int64;
      LMerge: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LE: int64;
    begin
      if self.FHeader = self.FLatch then
        return false;
      end;
      LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(self.FModule, self.FHeaderId);
      if LTerm.Kind <> IROp.Branch then
        return false;
      end;
      LStayAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(LTerm.Targets[0]);
      LExitAt := self.FAnalysis.PositionOf(LTerm.Targets[1]);
      if (LStayAt < 0) or (LExitAt < 0) then
        return false;
      end;
      if self.FIn[LStayAt] and (not self.FIn[LExitAt]) then
        LStay := LTerm.Targets[0];
        LExit := LTerm.Targets[1];
      else
        if self.FIn[LExitAt] and (not self.FIn[LStayAt]) then
          LStay := LTerm.Targets[1];
          LExit := LTerm.Targets[0];
          LStayAt := LExitAt;
        else
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      if self.FAnalysis.PredsOf(LStayAt).Count <> 1 then
        return false;
      end;
      LInstrs := self.FModule.BlockAt(self.FHeaderId).Instrs;
      LCount := 0;
      for LK := 0 to LInstrs.Count - 1 do
        if self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LK]).Kind <> IROp.Phi then
          LCount := LCount + 1;
        end;
      end;
      if LCount > ADAM_LOOPS_ROTATE_SIZE then
        return false;
      end;
      // The header's copy before it, in its scopes: its phis are their preheader values
      LFirst := self.FModule.InsertBlock(self.FFunctionId, self.FHeader, true);
      LMap := ref Int64Map(ADAM_LOOPS_NONE);
      LValues := ref Int64List();
      for LK := 0 to LInstrs.Count - 1 do
        LId := LInstrs[LK];
        LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LId);
        if LInstr.Kind = IROp.Phi then
          for LE := 0 to LInstr.Targets.Count - 1 do
            if LInstr.Targets[LE] = self.FPreheaderId then
              LMap.Put(LId, LInstr.Operands[LE]);
            end;
          end;
          LValues.Add(LId);
          skip;
        end;
        LCopyId := self.FModule.Emit(LFirst, LInstr.Kind, LInstr.ValueType, LInstr.Node);
        LCopy := self.FModule.InstrAt(LCopyId);
        LCopy.CopyFieldsFrom(LInstr);
        // An operand is made before its use in the header: the map already has it
        for LE := 0 to LInstr.Operands.Count - 1 do
          LCopy.Operands.Add(DoMappedOf(LMap, LInstr.Operands[LE]));
        end;
        for LE := 0 to LInstr.Targets.Count - 1 do
          LCopy.Targets.Add(LInstr.Targets[LE]);
        end;
        LMap.Put(LId, LCopyId);
        if not IsTerminator(LInstr.Kind) then
          LValues.Add(LId);
        end;
      end;
      // The preheader runs into the copy; the header is entered from the latch alone
      DoRetarget(self.FModule, self.FPreheaderId, self.FHeaderId, LFirst);
      for LK := 0 to LInstrs.Count - 1 do
        LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LInstrs[LK]);
        if LInstr.Kind <> IROp.Phi then
          skip;
        end;
        LOperands := ref Int64List();
        LTargets := ref Int64List();
        for LE := 0 to LInstr.Targets.Count - 1 do
          if LInstr.Targets[LE] <> self.FPreheaderId then
            LOperands.Add(LInstr.Operands[LE]);
            LTargets.Add(LInstr.Targets[LE]);
          end;
        end;
        LInstr.Operands := LOperands;
        LInstr.Targets := LTargets;
      end;
      // The stay block's and the exit's phis take the copy's entries
      self.DoHeaderEntries(LStay, LMap, LFirst);
      self.DoHeaderEntries(LExit, LMap, LFirst);
      // A header value used where the header no longer dominates (past the stay block, or
      // a header phi's back edge entry): a phi of the stay block merges it with its copy
      for LI := 0 to LValues.Count - 1 do
        LId := LValues[LI];
        LInstr := self.FModule.InstrAt(LId);
        LUses := self.FAnalysis.UsesOf(LId);
        LMerge := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
        for LK := 0 to LUses.Count - 1 do
          LUser := self.FModule.InstrAt(LUses[LK]);
          if (LUser.Block = self.FHeaderId) and (LUser.Kind <> IROp.Phi) then
            skip;
          end;
          if (LUser.Block = LStay) and (LUser.Kind = IROp.Phi) then
            skip;
          end;
          for LE := 0 to LUser.Operands.Count - 1 do
            if LUser.Operands[LE] <> LId then
              skip;
            end;
            // An entry on an edge from the header itself keeps the header's value
            if (LUser.Kind = IROp.Phi) and (LUser.Targets[LE] = self.FHeaderId) then
              skip;
            end;
            if LMerge = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
              LMerge := DoNewPhi(self.FModule, LStay, LInstr.ValueType, LInstr.Node);
              LMergePhi := self.FModule.InstrAt(LMerge);
              LMergePhi.Operands.Add(DoMappedOf(LMap, LId));
              LMergePhi.Targets.Add(LFirst);
              LMergePhi.Operands.Add(LId);
              LMergePhi.Targets.Add(self.FHeaderId);
            end;
            LUser.Operands[LE] := LMerge;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      ARotated := LStay;
      return true;
    end;

    // The loop unswitched (see the header) on the first branch of it whose condition is
    // made outside it (no constant), when it has at most ADAM_LOOPS_UNSWITCH_SIZE
    // instructions: a copy where the condition is false, the loop's own where it is true,
    // the preheader's jump a branch on it between their headers
    hidden method DoUnswitch(): bool;
    var
      LExits: ref Int64List;
      LBlocks: ref Int64Map;
      LValues: ref Int64Map;
      LTerm: ref IRInstr;
      LPreTerm: ref IRInstr;
      LCondition: int64;
      LBranchBlock: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.FSize > ADAM_LOOPS_UNSWITCH_SIZE then
        return false;
      end;
      LBranchBlock := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      LCondition := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
      for LI := 0 to self.FBlocks.Count - 1 do
        LTerm := DoTerminatorOf(self.FModule, self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FBlocks[LI]));
        if LTerm.Kind <> IROp.Branch then
          skip;
        end;
        LCondition := LTerm.Operands[0];
        if self.DoInLoop(LCondition) or
          (self.FModule.InstrAt(LCondition).Kind = IROp.Constant) then
          skip;
        end;
        LBranchBlock := self.FAnalysis.BlockAt(self.FBlocks[LI]);
        leave;
      end;
      if LBranchBlock = ADAM_LOOPS_NONE then
        return false;
      end;
      LPreTerm := DoTerminatorOf(self.FModule, self.FPreheaderId);
      if LPreTerm.Kind <> IROp.Jump then
        return false;
      end;
      LExits := self.DoExits();
      LBlocks := ref Int64Map(ADAM_LOOPS_NONE);
      LValues := ref Int64Map(ADAM_LOOPS_NONE);
      self.DoCloneLoop(LBlocks, LValues);
      self.DoExitEntries(LExits, LBlocks, LValues);
      self.DoSetCondition(LBranchBlock, true);
      self.DoSetCondition(LBlocks.Find(LBranchBlock), false);
      // The condition made outside the loop dominates the preheader's end (the preheader
      // is the header's one way in): it picks the loop
      LPreTerm.Kind := IROp.Branch;
      LPreTerm.Operands.Add(LCondition);
      LPreTerm.Targets.Add(LBlocks.Find(self.FHeaderId));
      return true;
    end;

    // One shape for the first loop that takes one, in this order: unswitching, a full
    // unroll, a rotation, a partial unroll; each tried once per loop header (a rotated
    // loop's new header counts as rotated, a fully unrolled one as rotated too); false when
    // no loop takes any
    hidden method DoShapeOne(): bool;
    var
      LRotated: int64;
      LHeader: int64;
      LL: int64;
    begin
      for LL := 0 to self.FAnalysis.LoopCount() - 1 do
        if not self.DoTake(LL) then
          skip;
        end;
        LHeader := self.FHeaderId;
        if self.FUnswitched.IndexOf(LHeader) < 0 then
          self.FUnswitched.Add(LHeader);
          if self.DoUnswitch() then
            return true;
          end;
        end;
        if self.FUnrolled.IndexOf(LHeader) < 0 then
          if self.DoFullUnroll() then
            self.FUnrolled.Add(LHeader);
            self.FRotated.Add(LHeader);
            return true;
          end;
        end;
        if self.FRotated.IndexOf(LHeader) < 0 then
          self.FRotated.Add(LHeader);
          LRotated := ADAM_LOOPS_NONE;
          if self.DoRotate(LRotated) then
            self.FRotated.Add(LRotated);
            return true;
          end;
        end;
        if self.FUnrolled.IndexOf(LHeader) < 0 then
          self.FUnrolled.Add(LHeader);
          if self.DoPartialUnroll() then
            return true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // loopshape over the function, at most ADAM_LOOPS_MAX_SHAPES shapes, the facts and the
    // loop form made again after each; true when anything changed
    method Run(): bool;
    var
      LChanged: bool;
    begin
      LChanged := false;
      while self.FShapes < ADAM_LOOPS_MAX_SHAPES do
        if not self.DoShapeOne() then
          leave;
        end;
        LChanged := true;
        self.FShapes := self.FShapes + 1;
        self.FAnalysis := ref FunctionAnalysis(self.FModule, self.FFunctionId,
          ADAM_OPT_FACTS_LOOPS | ADAM_OPT_FACTS_USES);
        if FormLoops(self.FModule, self.FFunctionId, self.FAnalysis) then
          self.FAnalysis := ref FunctionAnalysis(self.FModule, self.FFunctionId,
            ADAM_OPT_FACTS_LOOPS | ADAM_OPT_FACTS_USES);
        end;
      end;
      return LChanged;
    end;
  end;

// The pass loopshape (see the header) over AModule's function AFunction with its analysis
// AAnalysis: the loop form first (FormLoops), then each innermost loop unswitched,
// unrolled or rotated; true when it changed the function
public func ShapeLoops(const AModule: ref IRModule; const AFunction: int64;
  const AAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis): bool;
var
  LAnalysis: ref FunctionAnalysis;
  LShaper: ref LoopShaper;
  LChanged: bool;
begin
  if AAnalysis.LoopCount() = 0 then
    return false;
  end;
  LChanged := FormLoops(AModule, AFunction, AAnalysis);
  LAnalysis := AAnalysis;
  if LChanged then
    LAnalysis := ref FunctionAnalysis(AModule, AFunction,
      ADAM_OPT_FACTS_LOOPS | ADAM_OPT_FACTS_USES);
  end;
  LShaper := ref LoopShaper(AModule, AFunction, LAnalysis);
  if LShaper.Run() then
    LChanged := true;
  end;
  return LChanged;
end;

end.
